{"raw": {"https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260925018": {"title": "Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Design (two posts)", "description": "Job Application - Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Design (two posts) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification School of Design Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Design (two posts) (Ref. 260925018) The School of Design, a leading and transdisciplinary design school, is at the forefront of nurturing capable, open-minded, creative talents and active learners; contributing to innovation in Hong Kong and the Chinese Mainland while maintaining a global perspective. \u00a0As one of the top design schools in the world, its highly diverse design expertise widely covers Product Design, Interaction Design, Information Design, Advertising Design, Media Design, Interior Design, Environmental Design, Social Design, Service Design, Transitional Environments Design, Innovative Business Design, Intelligent Systems Design, Smart Service Design and Innovative Multimedia Entertainment. \u00a0It is consistently ranked among the top 25 on the Quacquarelli Symonds (QS) World University Rankings by Subject - Art and Design. \u00a0The School is based in a Zaha Hadid designed building well-equipped for innovative research and creative learning on the university campus. \u00a0Please visit the website at https://www.sd.polyu.edu.hk/en/ for more information about the School. The School attaches equal importance to design theory and application, integrates art with science, actively promotes interdisciplinary cooperation and learning, emphasises high-quality design education, conducts high-level research, and provides consulting services. \u00a0The School is committed to contributing its expertise to the community through applied research and consultancy, providing forward-looking advice and support to the industry covering three main pillars: Design Intelligence, Design for Virtue, and Design Wellbeings; and contributes to innovation in Hong Kong and the Chinese Mainland, while maintaining a global perspective. The School is looking for candidates who will work in a transdisciplinary design environment that builds on the School\u2019s global position within the regional and Chinese context (e.g. the Greater Bay Area). More specifically, candidates are sought, preferably with industry experience together with a strong track record of teaching and research in any one of the following areas: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Communication Design (e.g. \u00a0strategy, branding, creative advertising, market research, content creation, information design, infographics, wayfinding) \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Content Design (e.g. digital content creation, digital communication design, brand development, publication design) \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Design for Entrepreneurship (e.g. \u00a0 \u00a0design strategy, user-centred design, design management, circular design, product service systems) \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Immersive Media and Game Design (e.g. animation content creation, filmmaking, storytelling, game design, game programming, interactive storytelling, XR, virtual production, AIGC, arts and technology) \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Interactive System Design (e.g. \u00a0UX design, smart product, design for AI, internet of things, digital fabrication, data driven design) \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Service Design and Social Innovation (e.g. \u00a0strategic innovation, user experience design, organisational/community design) \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Interaction Design (e.g. \u00a0design-oriented HCI, user experience and interface design, research through design, design methodologies, interactive computing) Candidates are expected to demonstrate a strong research potential and/or good publication track record in transdisciplinary design projects (e.g. \u00a0healthcare systems, smart tourism, e-enterprises, city-regeneration, age-friendly city, etc.). Duties The appointees will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0synthesise knowledge and design applications with theories, design research methods and form-giving techniques; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0provide leadership in all aspects of academic activities, including research, teaching and service among the design disciplines; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0teach at undergraduate and/or postgraduate levels in a mix of design disciplines; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0act as student advisor and supervisor to groups as well as individual students including research students; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0secure competitive research grants and conduct research that leads to publications in refereed journals, or a body of design work which leads to outputs contributing to the knowledge and teaching of the design disciplines; (f)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0engage actively in research and scholarly activities serving the regional and international industry with significance and relevance to the discipline and profession; (g) \u00a0 \u00a0work with industry, nonprofits and the public sector to initiate funded research projects; (h) \u00a0 \u00a0activate inter-departmental and inter-institutional collaboration and networking; and (i)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Dean of School or his delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0a relevant PhD degree with professional and/or teaching experiences in a specialised area of design and/or a related discipline; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0extensive knowledge of and expertise in an area of design with hands-on techniques; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0extensive knowledge of and track record in design research and research methodologies; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0a high level of contextual and cultural awareness, and a vision for the future development of the profession; and (e) \u00a0 \u00a0a strong commitment to excellence in teaching, research and professional service. Applicants for appointment at Associate Professor level should have stronger relevant academic and/or professional achievements. \u00a0Candidates with less experience may be considered for appointment at a lower level. Applicants should submit (a) a letter of application declaring a focus area of expertise; (b) updated curriculum vitae; (c) a brief statement of research and teaching philosophy; (d) three key publications; and (e) a design and/or teaching portfolio including samples of personal and professional work. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.\u00a0 Initial appointment for Assistant Professor will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.\u00a0 Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement.\u00a0 An appropriate term will be provided for appointment at\u00a0Associate Professor level.\u00a0 For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . Consideration of applications will commence on 31 October 2026 until the positions are filled. Apply Now Posting date: 25 September 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260921002": {"title": "Associate Professor in Fashion and Textile Technology", "description": "Job Application - Associate Professor in Fashion and Textile Technology Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification School of Fashion and Textiles Associate Professor in Fashion and Textile Technology (Ref. 260921002) The School of Fashion and Textiles (SFT) was established in 2022 as an independent school, extending the lineage from the Institute of Textiles and Clothing (ITC) with 65 years of history at The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. SFT carries and leverages its proud history of research and curricular excellence, innovation and creativity, and entrepreneurship to be the top fashion school for nurturing and cultivating global fashion leaders for the future. With rapid technological advancement, fashion is ever-expanding, with so many permutation and integration possibilities encompassing different aspects of society and humanities to contribute to knowledge advancement, reimagining the future, and betterment of society. \u00a0SFT is seeking internationally excellent candidates to meet the growing demand and explore creative possibilities. Please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/sft/ for further information about the School. Duties The appointee will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0teach, supervise research students, and contribute to curriculum development at both undergraduate and postgraduate levels; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0initiate, lead and participate in research, consultancy and other scholarly activities leading to publications in refereed journals, exhibitions and the securing of research grants; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0undertake academic, departmental and institutional administrative duties; and (d) \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Dean of the School or her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0a PhD in Fashion or Textile Technology or a closely related discipline with substantial relevant post-qualification experience; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0demonstrated expertise in university teaching and research in areas related to fashion and textile technology; (c) an excellent research and publication record in high impact scholarly journals, along with a proven track record (or demonstrated potential) in securing research grants and externally funded projects; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0a strong commitment to excellence in teaching, research and professional/community service; and (e) \u00a0 \u00a0excellent communication skills, with the ability to use English as the medium of instruction. Preference will be given to candidates with a strong research orientation and a proven teaching track record. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.\u00a0 An appropriate term will be provided for appointment at Associate Professor level. For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . Consideration of applications will commence on 30 September 2026 until the position is filled. Apply Now Posting date: 21 September 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260915003": {"title": "Chair Professor / Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Sustainable Ocean Science and Engineering under Strategic Hiring Scheme", "description": "Job Application - Chair Professor / Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Sustainable Ocean Science and Engineering under Strategic Hiring Scheme Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering Chair Professor / Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Sustainable Ocean Science and Engineering under Strategic Hiring Scheme (Ref. 260915003) The Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering at PolyU enjoys a high international reputation in conducting world-class research for societal benefits and has well established partnerships with the industry and government agencies in Hong Kong and beyond. It is ranked the 2nd best worldwide in Civil Engineering in the U.S. News Best Global Universities Rankings 2026, the 18th in Civil and Structural Engineering and the 34th in Environmental Science in the QS World University Rankings by Subject 2026 (both ranked No. 1 in Hong Kong). The Department offers academic programmes at various levels (PhD, MSC, BEng, BSc). The Department currently has about 80 faculty members (more than 40 regular faculty members at Assistant Professor and above levels) and around 40 technical and administrative personnel, and is committed to international standards of excellence in teaching and research. Please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/cee/ for more information about the Department. The Hong Kong Special Administrative Region is an international city located strategically at the heart of Asia and is the gateway to Chinese Mainland, with excellent transport links to major international cities.\u00a0 The University\u2019s campus is located near the harbour connecting Kowloon and the Hong Kong Island, and in the vicinity of Tsim Sha Tsui, which is the most popular area for visitors. The Department is seeking a highly motivated and suitably qualified individual with research expertise in climate modelling, atmospheric dynamics, hydrometeorology, or other related climate science disciplines. To boost the leadership and impact of PolyU\u2019s research work in areas of significant societal needs and strategic importance, the Strategic Hiring Scheme is introduced to recruit faculty members at all levels and outstanding scholars are invited to join the University under the Strategic Hiring Scheme.\u00a0 Appointees recruited under the Strategic Hiring Scheme should have conducted / led world-leading research that is commensurate with the stage of their academic career. Duties The appointees will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0teach at undergraduate and postgraduate levels in related disciplines; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0conduct research that leads to publications in top-tier refereed journals and awards of research grants; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0undertake research, programme / curriculum development and administration; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0supervise student projects and theses; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0engage in industrial and scholarly research / consultancy activities; (f)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0undertake academic and departmental administrative duties; and (g) \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Unit or his delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0a PhD in Engineering or Science, specialising in Coastal / Ocean Engineering, Ocean Science and Climatology, Hydraulic / Hydrological Engineering, Marine Technology, or a related field; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0a strong commitment to excellence in teaching and research; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0strong records of research, publications and scholarship in coastal modelling, marine technology, ocean renewables and sustainability, and/or ocean dynamics; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0good networking ability and excellent potential to become a world-leading scholar; and (e) \u00a0 \u00a0excellent communication skills and the ability to use English as the medium of instruction. Applicants for appointment at Chair Professor level should have an outstanding record of global leadership and research achievement in the community, in addition to substantial years of relevant post-qualification experience. Applicants for appointment at Professor or Associate Professor level should have a substantial number of years of experience and an excellent record of relevant academic and/or research achievement in the specified field. \u00a0Applicants with less experience will be considered for appointment at the level of Assistant Professor. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered. \u00a0Faculty members recruited through the Strategic Hiring Scheme at Chair Professor or Professor level will receive a start-up grant of HKD 5 million or more to support research activities (including the admission of two PhD students, purchase of equipment, hiring of research staff, etc.) in the initial five years, whereas those appointed at Associate Professor or Assistant Professor level will receive a start-up grant of HKD 3 million or more.\u00a0 Initial appointment for Assistant Professor will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.\u00a0 Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement.\u00a0\u00a0An appropriate term will be provided for appointment at Associate Professor / Professor / Chair Professor levels.\u00a0 For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . Consideration of applications will commence on 14 October 2026 until the positions are filled. Apply Now Posting date: 15 September 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260904007": {"title": "Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Hospitality Management, Tourism Management, Event Management or Information Technology in Hospitality & Tourism", "description": "Job Application - Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Hospitality Management, Tourism Management, Event Management or Information Technology in Hospitality & Tourism Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification School of Hotel and Tourism Management Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Hospitality Management, Tourism Management, Event Management or Information Technology in Hospitality & Tourism (Ref. 260904007) The School of Hotel and Tourism Management (SHTM) at The Hong Kong Polytechnic University seeks a qualified faculty member at the rank of Associate Professor or Assistant Professor to join its dynamic faculty of more than 90 members drawn from around 20 countries and regions. The SHTM sets itself apart from other hospitality and tourism educational institutions by consistently earning a high standing in the upper echelons of international rankings. Placed No. 1 in the world in the \u201cHospitality and Tourism Management\u201d category in ShanghaiRanking\u2019s Global Ranking of Academic Subjects 2025 for the ninth consecutive year, ranked No. 1 globally in the \u201cCommerce, Management, Tourism and Services\u201d category in the University Ranking by Academic Performance in 2024/2025 for eight years in a row, rated No. 1 in the world in the \u201cHospitality, Leisure, Sport & Tourism\u201d subject area by the CWUR Rankings by Subject 2017, and ranked No. 2 globally among comprehensive universities in the \u201cHospitality and Leisure Management\u201d subject area in the QS World University Rankings by Subject 2026, the SHTM is a symbol of excellence in the field, exemplifying its motto of Leading Hospitality and Tourism . \u00a0The Hong Kong Polytechnic University is among the world\u2019s top 100 universities (No. 50 in QS World University Rankings 2027 and No. 80 in Times Higher Education World University Rankings 2026). The School currently enrols more than 1,500 students from close to 50 countries and regions around the world, offering a comprehensive range of programmes from bachelor\u2019s and master\u2019s degrees to professional doctoral (Doctor of Hotel and Tourism Management) and Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) programmes. \u00a0Through Hotel ICON ( www.hotel-icon.com ), the School\u2019s groundbreaking teaching and research hotel and a vital aspect of its paradigm-shifting approach to hospitality and tourism education, the SHTM is advancing teaching, learning and research, inspiring a new generation of passionate, pioneering professionals to take their positions as leaders in the hospitality and tourism industry.\u00a0 Please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/shtm/ for more information about the School. Duties The appointee will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0teach and contribute to curriculum development at undergraduate and/or postgraduate levels and supervise doctoral research; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0conduct impactful research that leads to publications in top-tier refereed journals, awards of external research grants, and meaningful societal impact; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0initiate, lead and participate in knowledge-transfer activities and other scholarly activities; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0undertake academic administration duties and departmental service; and (e) \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Dean of the School or his delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0normally a PhD degree or equivalent in Hospitality, Tourism, Business or a related discipline; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0demonstrated potential for excellent teaching and research excellence; and (c) \u00a0 \u00a0substantial industry experience related to the position. Applicants for appointment at Associate Professor level should have substantial university teaching experience and an excellent portfolio of teaching in respective areas, and demonstrated academic leadership in hospitality and tourism through research as evidenced by publications in top rated journals, awards of research grants, scholarship and high-level consultancy in respective areas. Preferences will be given to candidates with a track record of research and expertise in smart technology applications, AI, robotics, big data analytics and innovations/entrepreneurship as related to hospitality, tourism and/or event management. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered. \u00a0Initial appointment for Assistant Professor will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.\u00a0 Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement.\u00a0\u00a0An appropriate term will be provided for appointment at\u00a0Associate Professor level.\u00a0 For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . In addition to a highly competitive compensation package, a start-up research fund and staff development support can be provided to the qualified appointees. \u00a0Appointee is paid on a monthly basis for 12 months annually. Consideration of applications will commence on 15 September 2026 until the position is filled. Apply Now Posting date: 4 September 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260903016": {"title": "Instructor", "description": "Job Application - Instructor Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification School of Hotel and Tourism Management Instructor (Ref. 260903016) Duties The appointee will be required to participate in teaching, administration and development activities in Food and Beverage Management (including wine-related subjects). Qualifications Applicants should have: (a)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0a relevant master\u2019s degree or an equivalent professional qualification plus at least three \u00a0 \u00a0 years\u2019 teaching or industry experience; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0 good subject knowledge, skills and competence in related discipline(s), including international cuisines; and (c) \u00a0 \u00a0 excellent English and communication skills. Preference will be given to those with a degree/diploma in Culinary Arts or an equivalent qualification. Possession of relevant teaching experience in tertiary institutions and recognised food and/or beverage certificates, i.e., wine certificates (WSET levels 1-4), Food Hygiene (level 2 or above), HACCAP, coffee certificates (SCAA, SCAE or other recognised certificates), first aid (basic, intermediate or advanced), and with front-of-house experience, will be an advantage. Please visit the website at www.polyu.edu.hk/htm for more information about the School. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.\u00a0 Initial appointment will be made on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.\u00a0 Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement. Consideration of applications will commence on 15 September 2026 until the position is filled . Apply Now Posting date: 3 September 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260901009": {"title": "Professor in Construction Automation", "description": "Job Application - Professor in Construction Automation Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Construction Management and Intelligence Professor in Construction Automation (Ref. 260901009) The Department of Construction Management and Intelligence is one of the constituent departments of the Faculty of Construction and Environment. The Department offers a full range of programmes leading to the awards of Doctor of Philosophy, Master of Philosophy, Master of Science and Bachelor of Science. It has an undergraduate student body of over 600 full-time students and a postgraduate student body of over 300. The Department currently has a total of 25 full-time academic staff, 20 technical and administrative staff and over 100 research personnel. The Department is committed to excellence in teaching, research and service to the community. Please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/cmi/ for more information about the Department. The Department is looking for enthusiastic, established and suitably qualified person with a PhD degree to join the Department to take part in a number of teaching and research activities. Duties The appointee will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0conduct research in related areas and contribute to the development of the Department\u2019s strategic research area of Construction Automation / AI and Robotics for Construction and Construction Engineering; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0initiate, lead and participate in scholarly research in his/her area of expertise and be active in research leading to quality journal publications and in bidding for external research grants and projects; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0be responsible for developing externally-funded research programme by supervising / coaching students at bachelor / master / PhD / doctoral degree level; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0contribute to the success of the Department by initiating new internal and external collaborations and proactive participation; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0undertake teaching duties in the relevant subject areas at undergraduate and postgraduate levels; (f)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0participate in programme / curriculum planning, development and administration of undergraduate and postgraduate programmes; (g) \u00a0 \u00a0mentor and nurture the next generation of scholars and researchers; (h) \u00a0 \u00a0undertake relevant administrative duties; and (i)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Unit or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0have a PhD in Civil Engineering, Construction Engineering or a closely related field, with a focus on Construction Automation / AI and Robotics for Construction or related areas; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0have a strong commitment to excellence in teaching and academic advising; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0have a proven record in research and scholarship achievement; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0possess effective classroom teaching skills and good interpersonal skills; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0have experience in acquiring external research funding, including national, international funding bodies and industries; and (f) \u00a0 \u00a0have excellent communication, organisation, leadership and strong cooperation skills, and the ability to work in an interdisciplinary team. Applicants are expected to possess distinguished academic credentials with internationally prominent research and teaching track record. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered. \u00a0An appropriate term will be provided for appointment at Professor level.\u00a0 For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . Consideration of applications will commence on 15 September 2026 until the position is filled . Apply Now Posting date: 1 September 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260825005": {"title": "Professor in Supply Chain and Operations Management", "description": "Job Application - Professor in Supply Chain and Operations Management Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Logistics and Maritime Studies Professor in Supply Chain and Operations Management (Ref. 260825005) The Department of Logistics and Maritime Studies is one of the constituent departments of the Faculty of Business.\u00a0 The Department offers a full range of degree programmes in supply chain and operations management, maritime studies and others.\u00a0 The Department takes a multi-disciplinary approach to establishing an area of excellence in logistics, supply chain, and operations management.\u00a0 It strives to be a key player in Hong Kong\u2019s pursuit to become an international logistics hub. The Department\u2019s research portfolio lies in both academic and applied research.\u00a0 Professional services to industries are also provided by the academic staff in the form of consultancy in such areas as efficiency and quality improvement studies, market and operational analyses, optimisation, production, purchasing, and supply chain management.\u00a0 The Department also runs various self-financed programmes tailor-made to meet specific industry needs. Please visit the website at http://www.lms.polyu.edu.hk for more information about the Department. Duties The appointee will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0undertake teaching duties at various levels in the area of Supply Chain and Operations Management; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0supervise undergraduate and postgraduate research projects and theses; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0conduct research in related areas and contribute to the development of the Department\u2019s research strengths; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0initiate, lead and participate in scholarly research in their areas of expertise and be active in research leading to quality journal publications and in bidding for external research grants and applied research projects; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0engage in programme/curriculum planning, development and administration; (f)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0undertake relevant administrative duties; and (g) \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Department or his delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0a PhD degree in a related discipline; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0substantial years of relevant post-qualification and solid experience in teaching and a strong commitment to excellence in teaching and research; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0an excellent record of relevant academic and/or research achievements; and (d) \u00a0 \u00a0qualities of creativity, initiative and leadership. Preference will be given to those with prior business/managerial experience in related industries. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.\u00a0 An appropriate term will be provided for appointment at\u00a0Professor level.\u00a0 For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . Consideration of applications will commence on 1 September 2026 until the position is filled . Apply Now Posting date: 25 August 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260825004": {"title": "Associate Professor in Supply Chain and Operations Management", "description": "Job Application - Associate Professor in Supply Chain and Operations Management Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Logistics and Maritime Studies Associate Professor in Supply Chain and Operations Management (Ref. 260825004) The Department of Logistics and Maritime Studies is one of the constituent departments of the Faculty of Business. \u00a0The Department offers a full range of degree programmes in supply chain and operations management, maritime studies and others. \u00a0The Department takes a multi-disciplinary approach to establishing an area of excellence in logistics, supply chain, and operations management. \u00a0It strives to be a key player in Hong Kong\u2019s pursuit to become an international logistics hub. The Department\u2019s research portfolio lies in both academic and applied research. \u00a0Professional services to industries are also provided by the academic staff in the form of consultancy in such areas as efficiency and quality improvement studies, market and operational analyses, optimisation, production, purchasing, and supply chain management. \u00a0The Department also runs various self-financed programmes tailor-made to meet specific industry needs. Please visit the website at http://www.lms.polyu.edu.hk for more information about the Department. Duties The appointee will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0undertake teaching duties at various levels in the area of Supply Chain and Operations Management; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0supervise undergraduate and postgraduate research projects and theses; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0conduct research in related areas and contribute to the development of the Department\u2019s research strengths; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0initiate, lead and participate in scholarly research in their areas of expertise and be active in research leading to quality journal publications and in bidding for external research grants and applied research projects; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0engage in programme/curriculum planning, development and administration; (f)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0undertake relevant administrative duties; and (g) \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Department or his delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0a PhD degree in a related discipline; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0substantial years of relevant post-qualification and solid experience in teaching and a strong commitment to excellence in teaching and research; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0a proven record in research and scholarships; and (d) \u00a0 \u00a0qualities of creativity, initiative and leadership. Preference will be given to those with prior business/managerial experience in related industries. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.\u00a0 An appropriate term will be provided for appointment at\u00a0Associate Professor level.\u00a0 For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . Consideration of applications will commence on 1 September 2026 until the position is filled . Apply Now Posting date: 25 August 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260825003": {"title": "Assistant Professor in Supply Chain and Operations Management", "description": "Job Application - Assistant Professor in Supply Chain and Operations Management Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Logistics and Maritime Studies Assistant Professor in Supply Chain and Operations Management (Ref. 260825003) The Department of Logistics and Maritime Studies is one of the constituent departments of the Faculty of Business. \u00a0The Department offers a full range of degree programmes in supply chain and operations management, maritime studies and others. \u00a0The Department takes a multi-disciplinary approach to establishing an area of excellence in logistics, supply chain, and operations management. \u00a0It strives to be a key player in Hong Kong\u2019s pursuit to become an international logistics hub. The Department\u2019s research portfolio lies in both academic and applied research. \u00a0Professional services to industries are also provided by the academic staff in the form of consultancy in such areas as efficiency and quality improvement studies, market and operational analyses, optimisation, production, purchasing, and supply chain management. \u00a0The Department also runs various self-financed programmes tailor-made to meet specific industry needs. Please visit the website at http://www.lms.polyu.edu.hk for more information about the Department. Duties The appointee will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0undertake teaching duties at various levels in the area of Supply Chain and Operations Management; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0supervise undergraduate and postgraduate research projects and theses; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0conduct research in related areas and contribute to the development of the Department\u2019s research strengths; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0initiate, lead and participate in scholarly research in their areas of expertise and be active in research leading to quality journal publications and in bidding for external research grants and applied research projects; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0engage in programme/curriculum planning, development and administration; (f)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0undertake relevant administrative duties; and (g) \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Department or his delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0a PhD degree in a related discipline; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0solid experience in teaching and a strong commitment to excellence in teaching and research; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0a proven record in research and scholarships; and (d) \u00a0 \u00a0qualities of creativity, initiative and leadership. Preference will be given to those with prior business/managerial experience in related industries. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.\u00a0 Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.\u00a0 Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement.\u00a0 For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . Consideration of applications will commence on 1 September 2026 until the position is filled . Apply Now Posting date: 25 August 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260821001": {"title": "Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in AI/Robotics for Aircraft Maintenance / Low-Altitude Economy / Satellite and Space Engineering under Strategic Hiring Scheme (two posts)", "description": "Job Application - Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in AI/Robotics for Aircraft Maintenance / Low-Altitude Economy / Satellite and Space Engineering under Strategic Hiring Scheme  (two posts) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Aeronautical and Aviation Engineering Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in AI/Robotics for Aircraft Maintenance / Low-Altitude Economy / Satellite and Space Engineering under Strategic Hiring Scheme  (two posts) (Ref. 260821001) In line with the strategic development of the University and to lead the development of the aeronautical and aviation engineering discipline in teaching and research activities, the Department of Aeronautical and Aviation Engineering was established in the Faculty of Engineering. The Department currently offers undergraduate and postgraduate programmes and actively engages in various research and consultancy work. Please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/aae/ for more information about the Department. To boost the leadership and impact of PolyU\u2019s research work in areas of significant societal needs and strategic importance, the Strategic Hiring Scheme is introduced to recruit faculty members at all levels and outstanding scholars are invited to join the University under the Strategic Hiring Scheme.\u00a0 Appointees recruited under the Strategic Hiring Scheme should have conducted / led world-leading research that is commensurate with the stage of their academic career. The Department is seeking highly motivated and suitably qualified individuals with research expertise in AI/Robotics for Aircraft Maintenance / Low-Altitude Economy / Satellite and Space Engineering and applications are now invited from academics who are actively involved in the aforementioned strategic research track to fill the vacancies for academic staff under Strategic Hiring Scheme. Duties The appointees will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0undertake teaching duties at undergraduate and postgraduate levels in the aforementioned strategic research areas. \u00a0Beyond these primary areas, the candidate should be prepared to contribute to multidisciplinary subjects; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0conduct research that leads to publications in top-tier refereed journals; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0attract research fundings and support industrial researches; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0supervise student projects and theses; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0engage in scholarly research/consultancy in their area of expertise; (f)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0contribute to departmental services and activities; and (g) \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Unit or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0have a doctoral degree in Engineering with expertise in (1) AI/Robotics for aircraft maintenance, including but not limited to predictive maintenance, digital twins, conditional monitoring, robots for inspection and repairing; (2) in satellite and space engineering, including but not limited to spacecraft dynamics and control, payload and instrumentation, space robots, spacecraft design and tests, space technology applications such as navigation, remote sensing, and communications; or (3) in low-altitude economy, including but not limited to unmanned aerial vehicles, advanced air mobility, perception, autonomous control, decision making, unmanned air traffic management, and applications (e.g. transportation, inspection, search and rescue, etc.); (b) \u00a0 \u00a0have the relevant postdoctoral research experience and a publication record that is commensurate with the level of appointment; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0demonstrate excellence in original research and strong fundamental knowledge in one or more of the above-mentioned core research areas; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0demonstrate potential to establish significant externally funded research programmes; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0be able to demonstrate evidence of effective classroom teaching skills; and (f) \u00a0 \u00a0have excellent communication skills and the ability to use English as the medium of instruction. Applicants for appointment at Professor or Associate Professor level should have a substantial number of years of experience and an excellent record of relevant academic and/or research achievement in the specified field. Applicants with less experience will be considered for appointment at the level of Assistant Professor. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered. \u00a0Faculty members recruited through the Strategic Hiring Scheme at Chair Professor or Professor level will receive a start-up grant of HKD 5 million or more to support research activities (including the admission of two PhD students, purchase of equipment, hiring of research staff, etc.) in the initial five years, whereas those appointed at Associate Professor or Assistant Professor level will receive a start-up grant of HKD 3 million or more. Initial appointment for Assistant Professor will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract. \u00a0Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement.\u00a0 An appropriate term will be provided for appointment at Associate Professor / Professor levels. \u00a0For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . Consideration of applications will commence on 10 September 2026 until the positions are filled . Apply Now Posting date: 21 August 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260820014": {"title": "Instructor (Temporary Appointment) (two posts)", "description": "Job Application - Instructor (Temporary Appointment)  (two posts) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Chinese History and Culture Instructor (Temporary Appointment)  (two posts) (Ref. 260820014) [Appointment period: each for twelve months initially, with possibility of further appointment] Duties The appointees will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0engage in teaching aspects of Chinese History and Culture and undertake related pedagogical activities at undergraduate and postgraduate levels; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0engage in programme/curriculum design and development, consultancy projects and other scholarly activities that help promote the department\u2019s interests; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0provide administrative support for academic and departmental affairs; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0assist in organising student activities/training workshops to enhance students\u2019 learning experience; and (e) \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Department or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0a PhD degree in History or a relevant discipline; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0at least one year of relevant post-qualification teaching experience at the tertiary level; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0an excellent command of both English and Chinese (Putonghua), with fluency in Cantonese being an advantage; and (d) \u00a0 \u00a0a strong commitment to excellence in teaching and learning. Preference will be given to candidates with expertise in the fields of History, Literature, and Science and Technology. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered. Consideration of applications will commence on 2 September 2026 until the positions are filled. Apply Now Posting date: 20 August 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260818012": {"title": "Assistant Professor in Language Neuroscience and Neurotechnology", "description": "Job Application - Assistant Professor in Language Neuroscience and Neurotechnology Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Language Science and Technology Assistant Professor in Language Neuroscience and Neurotechnology (Ref. 260818012) The Department of Language Science and Technology (LST) is an academic unit within the Faculty of Humanities dedicated to the scientific study of language in all its facets. With a team over 70 committed academic and teaching/clinical staff members, our work spans from investigating the biological and cognitive foundations of language to its societal function in multilingual environments and its transformation through technology. The Department pursues interdisciplinary research that integrates core language science domains such as artificial intelligence and big data analytics, with applications in communication, education and healthcare. Alongside research activities, the Department actively translates scholarly insights into practice through clinical services, educational outreach and technology development that serve both local and international communities. The Department houses several specialised units, including the Speech Therapy Unit, the Research Centre for Language, Cognition and Neuroscience, and the Centre for Translation Studies, which serve as vital hubs for both research and practical application. More information about the Department can be found at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/lst/ . The Department invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position. We seek a scholar with strong expertise in integrating neuroscience and neurotechnology with language and speech data using computational approaches, including artificial intelligence, machine learning and deep learning, and a demonstrated commitment to translating research into clinical practice. We are particularly interested in candidates who: \u2022\u00a0 design and develop computational AI, machine learning or deep learning architectures to model language and speech processes at the neural level; \u2022\u00a0 use neurotechnological tools [e.g., EEG, MEG, fMRI, fNIRS, TMS, tDCS or brain-computer interfaces (BCI)] to investigate language and speech in typical and clinical populations; \u2022\u00a0 have a strong track record of research in language neuroscience, speech-language pathology or related fields, with clear clinical applications (e.g., aphasia, dyslexia, developmental language disorders or other communication and neurological conditions); and \u2022\u00a0 demonstrate excellence in translating research into clinical tools, neuro-rehabilitation protocols, assistive technologies, or digital therapeutics. Duties The appointee will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0contribute to the teaching/learning activities for the Department at undergraduate and postgraduate levels, and supervise student projects and theses; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0lead and/or participate in the planning, management and curriculum development; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0develop e-learning modules and design innovative pedagogy; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0secure external competitive research grants, conduct academic research, publish in top-tier refereed journals, and provide academic leadership in teaching, research and other scholarly activities; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0foster research collaborations both locally and internationally; (f) \u00a0 \u00a0engage the industries in high-level, impact-rich consultancies; (g) \u00a0 \u00a0carry out academic and administrative duties; and (h) \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Department or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0hold a PhD degree in a relevant field, such as Neuroscience, Linguistics, Cognitive Science, Speech-Language Pathology, Biomedical Engineering, Computer Science or a closely related field; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0demonstrate expertise in neuroscience and neurotechnology, as evidenced by publications and research experience using one or more of the following: \u2022\u00a0 Neuroimaging (e.g., f/MRI, EEG/MEG, fNIRS or ECoG); \u2022\u00a0 Neuromodulation (e.g., TMS, tDCS/tACs or DBS); \u2022\u00a0 Brain-Computer Interfaces (BCI) or assistive neurotechnologies; \u2022\u00a0 Computational modelling of neural signals; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0have a strong track record in designing and developing AI, machine learning, or deep learning models for language or speech data; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0have evidence of clinical translation or strong potential to translate research into clinical practice (e.g., aphasia, dyslexia, developmental language disorders or other communication and neurological conditions); (e) \u00a0 \u00a0have experience in teaching and curriculum development, with a willingness to contribute to programme planning and management; (f) \u00a0 \u00a0have a strong track record of publishing in high-quality international journals as a first or corresponding author, and demonstrated potential to secure competitive external research funding; (g) \u00a0 \u00a0be open to the use of e-learning and blended learning strategies in teaching and scholarship; and (h) \u00a0 \u00a0have good networking ability and interdisciplinary collaboration skills. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.\u00a0 Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.\u00a0 Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement.\u00a0 For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . Consideration of applications will commence on 17 September 2026 until the position is filled. Apply Now Posting date: 18 August 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260817003": {"title": "Clinical Associate in Radiography", "description": "Job Application - Clinical Associate in Radiography Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Health Technology and Informatics Clinical Associate in Radiography (Ref. 260817003) [will be conferred the title of Assistant Professor of Practice] Building on over 40 years of educational excellence in Hong Kong, the Department of Health Technology and Informatics (HTI) advances world-class teaching and research in four key medical fields (4M):\u00a0Medical Laboratory Science, Medical Imaging & Radiation Science, Medical Physics, and Medical Data Science. HTI cultivates future leaders with both professional expertise and scientific vision, fostering an inclusive learning environment that produces top graduates for Asia and beyond. At the forefront of innovation, HTI drives impactful research and technological breakthroughs in the 4M areas. Through cutting-edge scientific discovery and collaborations with leading global institutions, we deliver groundbreaking innovations with profound societal impact. Explore more: www.polyu.edu.hk/hti Duties The appointee will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0teach undergraduate/postgraduate courses and supervise students in their clinical training; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0perform other teaching support functions such as supervising students in projects and seminars; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0contribute to programme planning, administration and development; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0engage in teaching, learning and scholarly activities; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0carry out academic and administrative duties as required; and (f) \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Unit or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0a higher degree in Medical Imaging and Radiation Science (MIRS) or a related discipline; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0a qualification registrable with the Radiographers Board of the HKSAR; and (c) \u00a0 \u00a0not less than five years of post-registration clinical experience in Radiography. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.\u00a0 Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.\u00a0 Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement. Consideration of applications will commence on 24 August 2026 until the position is filled. Apply Now Posting date: 17 August 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260811002": {"title": "Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Occupational Therapy", "description": "Job Application - Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Occupational Therapy Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Rehabilitation Sciences Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Occupational Therapy (Ref. 260811002) The Department of Rehabilitation Sciences offers teaching programmes from entry-level BSc (Hons) to PhD for Occupational Therapy and Physiotherapy.\u00a0 There are over 70 faculty members in the disciplines of Occupational Therapy, Physiotherapy and Rehabilitation Sciences in the Department.\u00a0 The main translational research programmes in the Department are Better Ageing and Longevity, Intelligent Rehabilitation, Musculoskeletal and Sports Science, Neuroscience as well as Primary Healthcare and Lifestyle Medicine.\u00a0 It also operates a Rehabilitation Clinic which is the hub for clinical teaching and consultancy services to the community.\u00a0 The Department puts equal emphases on basic, applied and clinical research relevant to the theory and technology development in rehabilitation.\u00a0 Besides, the Department has taken the lead in incorporating Chinese therapeutics into the academic curricula which is unique worldwide.\u00a0 The vision of the Department is \u201c To build a future where individuals of all ages and abilities thrive through innovative rehabilitation \u201d.\u00a0 For more information about the Department, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/rs/ . Duties The appointee will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0undertake teaching in undergraduate and postgraduate programmes including supervision of student projects and seminars and/or supervision of clinical placements; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0carry out independent research and other scholarly activities and obtain research grants; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0participate in community, professional and/or consultancy services; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0undertake administrative duties; and (e) \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Unit or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0a PhD degree in Occupational Therapy and/or Artificial Intelligence or a related discipline; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0a strong commitment to excellence in teaching with demonstrated good teaching performance; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0a promising research and publication record with expertise of translational research in artificial intelligence, virtual reality, digital technologies or other emerging technologies relevant to rehabilitation and healthcare innovation; and (d) \u00a0 \u00a0good interpersonal and communication skills. Applicants with proven excellence in translational research and teaching may be considered for appointment at Associate Professor level or above. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered. \u00a0Initial appointment for Assistant Professor will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.\u00a0 Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement.\u00a0\u00a0An appropriate term will be provided for appointment at\u00a0Associate Professor / Professor levels.\u00a0 For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . Consideration of applications will commence on 25 August 2026 until the position is filled. Apply Now Posting date: 11 August 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260810008": {"title": "Teaching Fellow", "description": "Job Application - Teaching Fellow Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Chinese History and Culture Teaching Fellow (Ref. 260810008) [will be conferred the title of Lecturer] The Department of Chinese History and Culture is an academic department within the Faculty of Humanities.\u00a0 Its mission is to offer high-quality undergraduate and postgraduate\u00a0programmes that provide interdisciplinary training in the study of Chinese history and culture. Currently, the Department offers PhD and MPhil programmes, a taught-master degree programme, a major degree programme in Chinese History and Culture, a minor degree programme in Chinese History and Culture, and university-wide general education courses.\u00a0 The media of instruction are English and Putonghua.\u00a0 Please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/chc/ for more information about the Department. Duties The appointee will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0engage in teaching Chinese history and culture and undertake related pedagogical activities at undergraduate and postgraduate levels; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0engage in programme/curriculum design and development, consultancy projects and other scholarly activities that help promote the department\u2019s interests; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0provide administrative support for academic and departmental affairs; and (d) \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Department or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0a PhD degree in a relevant discipline; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0at least three years of relevant post-qualification tertiary teaching experience; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0strong commitment to excellence in teaching and learning; and (d) \u00a0 \u00a0an excellent command of both English and Chinese. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.\u00a0 Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.\u00a0 Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement. Consideration of applications will commence on 24 August 2026 until the position is filled. Apply Now Posting date: 10 August 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260810006": {"title": "Assistant Professor in Marketing (Consumer Behavior)", "description": "Job Application - Assistant Professor in Marketing (Consumer Behavior) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Management and Marketing Assistant Professor in Marketing (Consumer Behavior) (Ref. 260810006) The Department of Management and Marketing (MM) is one of the constituent departments of the Faculty of Business.\u00a0 MM is dedicated to providing cutting-edge knowledge and practical skills for our students in three key areas of business \u2014 Management , Marketing , and Management Information Systems .\u00a0 MM offers a full range of programmes leading to the awards of Doctor of Philosophy, Master of Science, and Bachelor of Business Administration.\u00a0 MM currently has around 60 full-time academic staff who are actively involved in research, consultancy, and management development work with businesses in Hong Kong, the Chinese mainland, and internationally.\u00a0 MM is committed to excellence in teaching, research and service to the community. The Marketing discipline of the Department invites applications for faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor, in the area of Consumer Behavior .\u00a0 The faculty members in the Marketing discipline of MM regularly publish their research in top-tier refereed marketing journals such as the Journal of Consumer Research, Journal of Marketing Research, Journal of Marketing, and Marketing Science .\u00a0 Research-focused applicants who are interested in joining our vibrant and growing research team are strongly encouraged to apply for the post. Please visit the website at https://mm.polyu.edu.hk/ for more information about MM.\u00a0 Applicants are invited to contact Professor Yuwei Jiang, Chair Professor and Associate Head of MM by email at yuwei.jiang@polyu.edu.hk for further information about the post. Duties The appointee will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0engage in top-level scholarly research in their areas of expertise; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0supervise research students; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0secure external competitive research grants; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0teach at the undergraduate and/or postgraduate levels; and (e) \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Unit or his delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0a PhD degree in Marketing or a relevant discipline at the time of appointment or be close to receiving it; and (b) \u00a0 \u00a0a strong research orientation and the potential to publish in high quality scholarly journals. Conditions of Service The compensation package, teaching loads, and research support are highly competitive. \u00a0Initial appointment for Assistant Professor will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.\u00a0 Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement.\u00a0 For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . C onsideration of applications will commence on 1 September 2026 until the position is filled . Apply Now Posting date: 10 August 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260803003": {"title": "Assistant Professor in Social Policy and Administration / Sociology, Anthropology and Philosophy", "description": "Job Application - Assistant Professor in Social Policy and Administration / Sociology, Anthropology and Philosophy Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Applied Social Sciences Assistant Professor in Social Policy and Administration / Sociology, Anthropology and Philosophy (Ref. 260803003) As one of the largest social sciences departments in the Asian Pacific region, the Department of Applied Social Sciences offers research degrees at MPhil and PhD levels as well as taught programmes at undergraduate and postgraduate levels in various disciplines. The Department is home to many thriving research and practice units: Centre for Social Policy and Social Entrepreneurship, Child Development Centre, China and Global Development Network, and Professional Practice and Assessment Centre. \u00a0It is also strongly connected with the Institute of Active Ageing of the Faculty of Health and Social Sciences and other health related disciplines. \u00a0They provide platforms for collaborative research, practice projects, and policy discussions with government departments and NGOs. \u00a0Focused areas of research in the Department include but not limited to: (a) family, child, youth and ageing studies; (b) psychology, mental health, and health; (c) social work and human service management; (d) social policy, social welfare, and community development; and (e) social theory, and the Chinese Mainland and global social development. Please visit the website at http://www.polyu.edu.hk/apss/ for more information about the Department. Duties The appointee will be required to: (a) teach subjects in the discipline of Social Policy and Administration / Sociology, Anthropology and Philosophy and/or related subjects; (b) contribute to the development and enhancement of teaching and learning; (c) lead and/or participate in the planning, management and curriculum development of undergraduate and postgraduate programmes; (d) develop e-learning modules and design innovative pedagogy; (e) secure external competitive research grants, conduct academic research, publish in good quality peer-reviewed journals, and provide academic leadership in teaching, research and other scholarly activities; (f) carry out academic and administrative duties as required; and (g) perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Unit or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should: (a) have a PhD degree in Social Policy and Administration / Sociology, Anthropology and Philosophy or other related disciplines; (b) have a solid academic background as well as research and teaching expertise in the Chinese Mainland\u2019s technological development and its impact on social development worldwide, including social impacts of AI and emerging technology, tech-driven social innovation, digital governance, and China\u2019s social development and role in a global context; (c) possess strong capabilities in one or more of the Department\u2019s existing core domains, including (i) social policy and accountability, with a focus on social policy analysis, social planning, comparative social policy, and health/labour/welfare policy; (ii) innovation and social development, with a focus on social entrepreneurship, labour and migration, and land and environment; and (iii) health, culture, and society, with a focus on sociology/anthropology of health, digital and techno-culture, and regional/area studies; (d) have proven track records in teaching and research; (e) have demonstrated record for establishing significant externally funded research programmes; (f) have considerable experience in academic programme planning, management and curriculum development; (g) demonstrate potential for research excellence, with proven ability to publish in high-quality journals being an advantage; (h) be open to the use of e-learning and blended learning strategies in teaching and scholarship; and (i) have local and international connections in research and professional capacities. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered. \u00a0Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.\u00a0 Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement.\u00a0 For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . Consideration of applications will commence on 17 August 2026 until the position is filled. Apply Now Posting date: 3 August 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260803001": {"title": "Instructor (Temporary Appointment)", "description": "Job Application - Instructor (Temporary Appointment) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Mechanical Engineering Instructor (Temporary Appointment) (Ref. 260803001) [Appointment period: twelve months] Duties The appointee will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0engage in a full range of activities related to teaching and learning, including preparing and developing materials, designing teaching and assessment strategies, delivering teaching in settings appropriate for the objective of learning, interacting with and motivating students, and assessing the performance of and giving feedback to students; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0assist in the development of subject curriculum and overall teaching and learning approach as well as in subject administration as required; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0assist in the activities pertaining to programme management; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0engage in departmental academic and administrative duties; and (e) \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Unit or his delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0a relevant master\u2019s degree plus at least one year of post-qualification tertiary or senior secondary teaching experience, and/or relevant professional, practical, or industrial experience; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0demonstrated promise of a high level of competence in teaching and carrying out subject administration responsibilities (and potential for contributing to curriculum/pedagogy development, subject and programme management and/or professional service if applicable); (c) \u00a0 \u00a0an excellent command of both written and spoken English; and (d) \u00a0 \u00a0good communication skills and the ability to use English as the medium of instruction. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered. Consideration of applications will commence on 10 August 2026 until the position is filled. Apply Now Posting date: 3 August 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260724015": {"title": "Part-time Visiting Lecturer (several posts)", "description": "Job Application - Part-time Visiting Lecturer (several  posts) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification School of Optometry Part-time Visiting Lecturer (several  posts) (Ref. 260724015) [Appointment period: tenable for 2026/2027 academic year] Duties The appointees will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0undertake teaching duties in the Master of Science in Vision Science and Innovation programme; and (b) \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of School or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have a doctoral degree, or a relevant first degree plus a higher degree and/or professional qualification in a relevant discipline and not less than three years of post-qualification teaching/research/practical and/or industrial experience. Conditions of Service The remuneration rate is from HK$900 to HK$1,000 per hour. Consideration of applications will commence on 31 July 2026 until the positions are filled. Apply Now Posting date: 24 July 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260724014": {"title": "Assistant Professor in Sports Science", "description": "Job Application - Assistant Professor in Sports Science Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Biomedical Engineering and Sports Technology Assistant Professor in Sports Science (Ref. 260724014) The Department of Biomedical Engineering (BME) is one of the five academic departments in the Faculty of Engineering, and it offers a full spectrum of BME programmes, from BSc, MSc to PhD. The team is the first group to offer Biomedical Engineering related undergraduate programme in Hong Kong, and has made great achievements in BME education, innovative research, and technology transfer. Currently BME has six thematic research areas, including Biomedical Imaging, Sensing, AI and Wearable Technology, Brain-Machine Interface and Neural Engineering, Molecular/Cellular Engineering and Biomaterials, Precision Diagnostics and Therapy, Prosthetics-Orthotics, Smart Ageing and Rehabilitation Engineering, and Sports Science and Technology. It aims to conduct cutting-edge research in these areas and nurture future leaders in prosthetics and orthotics, clinical engineering, medical instrumentation and sensors, and biological engineering by imparting interdisciplinary knowledge, innovative ideas, critical thinking and practical skills. Please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/bme for more information about the Unit. Duties The appointee will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0teach at undergraduate and postgraduate levels, and contribute to programme and curriculum development; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0initiate innovative research projects that leads to publications in top-tier refereed journals and awards of external research grants; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0supervise student projects and theses; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0engage in industrial and scholarly research/consultancy activities; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0undertake academic and departmental administrative duties; and (f) \u00a0 \u00a0 perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Unit or his delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0a PhD degree in relevant disciplines; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0strong commitment to excellence in teaching and research; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0published world-leading research as a main author; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0good networking ability; and (e) \u00a0 \u00a0excellent communication skills and the ability to use English as the medium of instruction. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.\u00a0 Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.\u00a0 Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement.\u00a0 For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . Consideration of applications will commence on 7 August 2026 until the position is filled. Apply Now Posting date: 24 July 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260724013": {"title": "Assistant Professor in Brain Machine Interface", "description": "Job Application - Assistant Professor in Brain Machine Interface Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Biomedical Engineering and Sports Technology Assistant Professor in Brain Machine Interface (Ref. 260724013) The Department of Biomedical Engineering (BME) is one of the five academic departments in the Faculty of Engineering, and it offers a full spectrum of BME programmes, from BSc, MSc to PhD. The team is the first group to offer Biomedical Engineering related undergraduate programme in Hong Kong, and has made great achievements in BME education, innovative research, and technology transfer. Currently BME has six thematic research areas, including Biomedical Imaging, Sensing, AI and Wearable Technology, Brain-Machine Interface and Neural Engineering, Molecular/Cellular Engineering and Biomaterials, Precision Diagnostics and Therapy, Prosthetics-Orthotics, Smart Ageing and Rehabilitation Engineering, and Sports Science and Technology. It aims to conduct cutting-edge research in these areas and nurture future leaders in prosthetics and orthotics, clinical engineering, medical instrumentation and sensors, and biological engineering by imparting interdisciplinary knowledge, innovative ideas, critical thinking and practical skills. Please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/bme for more information about the Unit. Duties The appointee will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0teach at undergraduate and postgraduate levels, and contribute to programme and curriculum development; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0initiate innovative research projects that leads to publications in top-tier refereed journals and awards of external research grants; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0supervise student projects and theses; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0engage in industrial and scholarly research/consultancy activities; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0undertake academic and departmental administrative duties; and (f) \u00a0 \u00a0 perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Unit or his delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0a PhD degree in relevant disciplines; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0strong commitment to excellence in teaching and research; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0published world-leading research as a main author; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0good networking ability; and (e) \u00a0 \u00a0excellent communication skills and the ability to use English as the medium of instruction. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered. \u00a0Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract. \u00a0Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement. \u00a0For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . Consideration of applications will commence on 7 August 2026 until the position is filled. Apply Now Posting date: 24 July 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260724007": {"title": "Assistant Professor in Satellite and Space Engineering", "description": "Job Application - Assistant Professor in Satellite and Space Engineering Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Aeronautical and Aviation Engineering Assistant Professor in Satellite and Space Engineering (Ref. 260724007) In line with the strategic development of the University and to lead the development of the aeronautical and aviation engineering discipline in teaching and research activities, the Department of Aeronautical and Aviation Engineering was established in the Faculty of Engineering. The Department currently offers undergraduate and postgraduate programmes and actively engages in various research and consultancy work. Please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/aae/ for more information about the Department. \u00a0Applications are now invited from academics who are actively involved in Satellite and Space Engineering to fill the vacancy for academic staff. Duties The appointee will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0initiate, lead and participate in scholarly research in his/her areas of expertise and be active in research leading to quality journal publications and in bidding for external research grants and applied research projects; (b)\u00a0 \u00a0 conduct research in satellite and space engineering and contribute to the development of the Department\u2019s research strengths; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0supervise undergraduate and postgraduate research projects and theses; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0undertake teaching duties at various levels in the area of satellite and space engineering; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0engage in programme/curriculum planning, development and administration; (f)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0undertake relevant administrative duties; and (g) \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Unit or his delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0a PhD degree in Engineering with expertise in satellite and space engineering, including but not limited to spacecraft dynamics and control, payload and instrumentation, space robots, spacecraft design and tests, space technology applications such as navigation, remote sensing, and communications; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0experience in acquiring external research funding including national and international funding bodies and industries; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0strong commitment to excellence in teaching and research; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0effective classroom teaching skills and good interpersonal skills; and (e) \u00a0 \u00a0excellent communication, organisational and leadership skills, as well as strong cooperation skills with the ability to work in an interdisciplinary team. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered. \u00a0Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.\u00a0 Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement.\u00a0\u00a0For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . Consideration of applications will commence on 10 August 2026 until the position is filled . Apply Now Posting date: 24 July 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260724006": {"title": "Assistant Professor in Low-Altitude Economy", "description": "Job Application - Assistant Professor in Low-Altitude Economy Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Aeronautical and Aviation Engineering Assistant Professor in Low-Altitude Economy (Ref. 260724006) In line with the strategic development of the University and to lead the development of the aeronautical and aviation engineering discipline in teaching and research activities, the Department of Aeronautical and Aviation Engineering was established in the Faculty of Engineering. The Department currently offers undergraduate and postgraduate programmes and actively engages in various research and consultancy work. Please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/aae/ for more information about the Department. \u00a0Applications are now invited from academics who are actively involved in Low-Altitude Economy to fill the vacancy for academic staff. Duties The appointee will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0initiate, lead and participate in scholarly research in his/her areas of expertise and be active in research leading to quality journal publications and in bidding for external research grants and applied research projects; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0conduct research in low-altitude economy and contribute to the development of the Department\u2019s research strengths; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0supervise undergraduate and postgraduate research projects and theses; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0undertake teaching duties at various levels in the area of low-altitude economy; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0engage in programme/curriculum planning, development and administration; (f)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0undertake relevant administrative duties; and (g) \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Unit or his delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0a PhD degree in Engineering with expertise in low-altitude economy, including but not limited to unmanned aerial vehicles, advanced air mobility, perception, autonomous control, decision making, unmanned air traffic management, and applications (e.g. transportation, inspection, search and rescue, etc.); (b) \u00a0 \u00a0experience in acquiring external research funding including national and international funding bodies and industries; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0strong commitment to excellence in teaching and research; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0effective classroom teaching skills and good interpersonal skills; and (e) \u00a0 \u00a0excellent communication, organisational and leadership skills, as well as strong cooperation skills with the ability to work in an interdisciplinary team. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered. \u00a0Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.\u00a0 Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement.\u00a0\u00a0For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . Consideration of applications will commence on 10 August 2026 until the position is filled . Apply Now Posting date: 24 July 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260724002": {"title": "Clinical Instructor", "description": "Job Application - Clinical Instructor Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification School of Nursing Clinical Instructor (Ref. 260724002) Established in 1977, the School of Nursing supports the mission of the University by nurturing graduates who are critical thinkers, effective communicators, innovative problem solvers, lifelong learners and ethical leaders. \u00a0It ranks 18th for the best School of Nursing internationally (QS Ranking 2026). \u00a0The education, research, consultancy and integrative health services are driven by a commitment to improve health of the community. \u00a0Currently, it has a total of around 80 full-time faculty members. \u00a0We welcome candidates from all nursing disciplines, including critical care, mental health, as well as prevention and infection control. Duties The appointee will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0supervise clinical projects and clinical practicum at undergraduate and postgraduate levels; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0teach pre-registration nursing programmes and supervise students in clinical/field studies; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0coordinate student clinical placement with local, national and overseas healthcare agencies; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0act as student advisor and counsellor; and (e) \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of School or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0a relevant master\u2019s degree plus not less than three years of post-qualification/post-registration clinical experience in local hospitals; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0a Certificate of Registration (Part I and/or II) issued by The Nursing Board/Council of Hong Kong; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0a valid practising certificate issued by The Nursing Council of Hong Kong; and (d) \u00a0 \u00a0a good command of both written and spoken English and Chinese, with fluency in Cantonese. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered. \u00a0Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract. \u00a0Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement. Consideration of applications will commence on 7 August 2026 until the position is filled. Apply Now Posting date: 24 July 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260715008": {"title": "Part-time Visiting Lecturer", "description": "Job Application - Part-time Visiting Lecturer Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of English and Communication Part-time Visiting Lecturer (Ref. 260715008) [Appointment period: from September 2026 to January 2027] Duties The appointee will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0teach subject(s) for the BA (Hons) in English and Applied Linguistics programme; and (b) \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of the Department or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0a doctoral degree in Applied Linguistics, Communication, Media Studies, Art History, Visual Arts or a related discipline with at least three years of post-qualification teaching experience; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0a good command of written and spoken English; and (c) \u00a0 \u00a0good communication skills. Conditions of Service The remuneration rate is HK$950 per hour. Consideration of applications will commence on 28 July 2026 until the position is filled. Apply Now Posting date: 15 July 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260713005": {"title": "Assistant Professor in Optimization and Operations Research / Statistics and Data Science/ Financial Mathematics / Engineering and Computational Mathematics / Mathematical Science / Actuarial Science", "description": "Job Application - Assistant Professor in Optimization and Operations Research / Statistics and Data Science/ Financial Mathematics / Engineering and Computational Mathematics / Mathematical Science / Actuarial Science Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Applied Mathematics Assistant Professor in Optimization and Operations Research / Statistics and Data Science/ Financial Mathematics / Engineering and Computational Mathematics / Mathematical Science / Actuarial Science (Ref. 260713005) The Department of Applied Mathematics (AMA) is one of the constituent departments of the Faculty of Computer and Mathematical Sciences. \u00a0Apart from making a significant contribution to most of other academic programmes of the University by providing service teaching, the Department also offers master programmes in Applied Mathematics for Science and Technology, Operational Research and Risk Analysis and Quantitative Finance and FinTech. \u00a0Starting from 2025/26 academic year, the Department offers a new Bachelor Scheme in Applied Mathematics and Finance Analytics and Fast-track Integrated Bachelor\u2019s and Master\u2019s Degree Programmes and will launch a new master programme, MSc in Mathematics for Artificial Intelligence Technology in 2026/27. \u00a0Members of the Department have expertise in applied optimization and optimal control, engineering computation, operational research, management science and applied statistics, FinTech, data science and machine learning. \u00a0There are currently 56 academic staff and about 154 research personnel in the Department. \u00a0Please visit the website at http://www.polyu.edu.hk/ama for more information about the Department. Duties The appointee will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0teach and contribute to curriculum development at undergraduate and postgraduate levels; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0supervise MPhil and PhD students; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0engage in scholarly research, consultancy and other scholarly activities leading to publications in top-tier refereed journals and award of research grants; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0undertake academic and departmental administrative duties; and (e) \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of the Department or his delegates. Qualifications Applicants should: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0have a PhD degree in Mathematics / Statistics / Financial Mathematics / Operations Research / Computational Mathematics / Applied Mathematics or a closely related field with experience in Data Science and Analytics; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0have expertise in applied statistics, operation research or mathematics; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0have an established track record in research and scholarship, including refereed publications and external grant applications; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0have a demonstrated commitment to excellence in teaching; and (e) \u00a0 \u00a0be highly proficient in written and spoken English. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.\u00a0 Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.\u00a0 Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement.\u00a0 For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . Consideration of applications will commence on 10 August 2026 until the position is filled. Apply Now Posting date: 13 July 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260624007": {"title": "Visiting Lecturer (Part-time) in Building Environment", "description": "Job Application - Visiting Lecturer (Part-time) in Building Environment Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Building Environment and Energy Engineering Visiting Lecturer (Part-time) in Building Environment (Ref. 260624007) [Appointment period: from September 2026 to May 2027] The Department of Building Environment and Energy Engineering (BEEE) contributes to PolyU\u2019s world ranking of 21st for Architecture and Built Environment and 18th for Civil and Structural Engineering in the QS World University Rankings by Subject 2026. BEEE is one of the constituent departments of the Faculty of Construction and Environment, and offers a full range of programmes leading to the awards of Doctor of Philosophy, Master of Philosophy, Master of Engineering, Master of Science and Bachelor of Engineering. Currently there are over 35 research staff and 190 research students (over 180 studying for PhD), over 600 full-time / part-time Master\u2019s students, an undergraduate student body of over 250 full-time students. \u00a0BEEE currently has over 50 full-time academic / teaching staff members engaging in a wide range of research activities organised in the following three themes: Building Energy : Energy issues in buildings addressed in the context of both demand and supply to promote sustainable built environments, urban energy systems and emerging clean energy technologies. Building Environment : Optimisation of buildings and built environments for thermal comfort, indoor air quality, visual / spatial and vibration / acoustic aspects to improve occupant health and productivity, and extraterrestrial human habitats. Building Safety and Resilience : Protection of building occupants from hazards such as fire and lightning to improve safety and resilience of communities, buildings and the built environments. The University and the Department strongly encourage a multi-cultural environment regarding both the staff and student body composition. Please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/beee/ for further information about the Department. Duties The appointee will be required to teach and conduct assessments in the daytime course \u201c Water System Engineering in Built Environments (BSE4312) \u201d to undergraduate students in Semester 2 of the 2026/2027 academic year. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0a PhD degree OR a master\u2019s degree in a related discipline with corporate membership in relevant professional bodies such as HKIE, CIBSE or CIPHE; (b)\u00a0 \u00a0 at least three years of post-qualification teaching / practical training experience in a related discipline; and (c) \u00a0 \u00a0a good command of written and spoken English, and strong communication skills. Conditions of Service The remuneration rate is HK$900 per hour. C onsideration of applications will commence on 8 July 2026 until the position is filled . Apply Now Posting date: 24 June 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260616018": {"title": "Teaching Fellow", "description": "Job Application - Teaching Fellow Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification School of Design Teaching Fellow (Ref. 260616018) [Appointment period: twelve months] Duties The appointee will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0assist in the development of new subjects for the Service Design programme, including contributing to the design of course content and assessments; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0collaborate with the academic team to ensure the curriculum aligns with industry standards and emerging trends in service design, customer experience (CX) and strategic design; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0provide input and insights based on expertise in service design methodologies to enhance the quality and relevance of the programme content; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0work closely with the programme coordinator and faculty members to facilitate a smooth transition into the new programme as well as offering support in various administrative and educational tasks; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0support in the preparation and coordination of the admission exercise for the Service Design programme, including reviewing applications, conducting interviews, and evaluating portfolios; (f)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0engage with prospective students to provide information about the programme, answer inquiries and assist with the admissions process; (g) \u00a0 \u00a0contribute to the planning and execution of promotional events and activities related to the Service Design programme; and (h) \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Dean of School or his delegates. Qualifications Applicants should: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0have a master\u2019s degree in a relevant field related to service design, strategic design, user experience (UX)/CX design, or human-centered design plus not less than five years of post-qualification experience in tertiary teaching and/or professional practice within the service design industry or innovation consulting; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0demonstrate expertise and proficiency in the following areas essential to service design: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0proficiency in service design tools and frameworks (e.g. customer journey mapping, service blueprinting, stakeholder mapping and persona development); \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0experience in both qualitative and quantitative design research methods (e.g. ethnographic research, in-depth interviews, co-creation workshops and usability testing); \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0knowledge of systems thinking and organisational design; \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0ability to design omni-channel service experiences by combining physical and digital touchpoints; \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0expertise in facilitating participatory design and co-design sessions with diverse stakeholders; and \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0proficiency in collaborative design and prototyping software (e.g. Figma, Miro, Mural, and Adobe Creative Cloud) tailored for service concept visualisation and prototyping. (c) \u00a0 \u00a0showcase the capacity to conduct tutorials, workshops and assessments within the service design and design thinking domain; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0demonstrate a keen ability to develop curriculum and convert materials to suit the unique requirements of service design and strategic innovation education; and (e) \u00a0 \u00a0possess exceptional oral and written communication skills as well as the ability to effectively engage with individuals from diverse backgrounds. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered. Consideration of applications will commence on 30 June 2026 until the position is filled . Apply Now Posting date: 16 June 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260616011": {"title": "Teaching Fellow (Temporary Appointment)", "description": "Job Application - Teaching Fellow (Temporary Appointment) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Division of Artificial Intelligence and the Humanities Teaching Fellow (Temporary Appointment) (Ref. 260616011) [Appointment period: twelve months initially, with possibility of further appointment] Duties The appointee will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0undertake teaching duties for the MSc in Generative AI and the Humanities programme, including the coordination and supervision of student seminars, tutorials and capstone projects/dissertation; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0engage in teaching, learning and scholarly activities; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0contribute to the planning, administration and development of programmes/courses; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0assist in organising student activities/training workshops to enhance students\u2019 learning experience; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0undertake administrative duties in academic and departmental affairs; and (f)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Division or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0a PhD degree in Computer Science or related disciplines; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0at least three years of post-qualification tertiary teaching experience and/or relevant professional, practical or industrial experience; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0good subject knowledge, skills and competence in the discipline; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0effective classroom teaching skills and a strong commitment to excellence in teaching and professional service; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0an excellent command of both written and spoken English; and (f)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0good communication and interpersonal skills. Applicants should also submit (i) an updated curriculum vitae; and (ii) a teaching statement elaborating his/her teaching philosophy and contribution for the position applied. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered. Consideration of applications will commence on 2 July 2026 until the position is filled. Apply Now Posting date: 16 June 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260608005": {"title": "Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Building Energy / Building Environment / Building Safety and Resilience under Strategic Hiring Scheme", "description": "Job Application - Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Building Energy / Building Environment / Building Safety and Resilience under Strategic Hiring Scheme Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Building Environment and Energy Engineering Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Building Energy / Building Environment / Building Safety and Resilience under Strategic Hiring Scheme (Ref. 260608005) The Department of Building Environment and Energy Engineering (BEEE) contributes to PolyU\u2019s world ranking of 17th for Architecture and Built Environment as well as Civil and Structural Engineering in the QS World University Rankings by Subject 2025. BEEE is one of the constituent departments of the Faculty of Construction and Environment, and offers a full range of programmes leading to the awards of Doctor of Philosophy, Master of Philosophy, Master of Engineering, Master of Science and Bachelor of Engineering. Currently there are over 35 research staff and 201 research students (187 studying for PhD), over 600 full-time / part-time Master\u2019s students, an undergraduate student body of over 250 full-time students. \u00a0BEEE currently has over 50 full-time academic / teaching staff members engaging in a wide range of research activities organised in the following three themes: Building Energy : Energy issues in buildings addressed in the context of both demand and supply to promote sustainable built environments, urban energy systems and emerging clean energy technologies. Building Environment : Optimisation of buildings and built environments for thermal comfort, indoor air quality, visual / spatial and vibration / acoustic aspects to improve occupant health and productivity, and Extraterrestrial human habitats. Building Safety and Resilience : Protection of building occupants from hazards such as fire and lightning to improve safety and resilience of communities, buildings and the built environments. The University and the Department strongly encourage a multi-cultural environment regarding both the staff and student body composition. Please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/beee/ for further information about the Department. BEEE is seeking internationally excellent candidate with exceptional track record of research and scholarship in the theme of Building Energy with preference to candidate demonstrating a strong and individualistic vision of the challenges facing modern urban environments and the opportunities afforded by emerging technologies to address them. To boost the leadership and impact of PolyU\u2019s research work in areas of significant societal needs and strategic importance, the Strategic Hiring Scheme is introduced to recruit faculty members at all levels and outstanding scholars are invited to join the University under the Strategic Hiring Scheme.\u00a0 Appointees recruited under the Strategic Hiring Scheme should have conducted / led world-leading research that is commensurate with the stage of their academic career. Duties The appointee will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0undertake teaching duties at various levels; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0supervise undergraduate and postgraduate research projects and theses; (c)\u00a0 \u00a0 conduct research in related areas and contribute to the development of the Department\u2019s research strength; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0initiate, lead and participate in scholarly research in his/her area of expertise and be active in research leading to quality journal publications and in bidding for external research grants and applied research projects; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0engage in programme / curriculum planning, administration and development; (f)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0provide leadership in developing a programme, a subject discipline or a research programme, etc.; (g) \u00a0 \u00a0undertake relevant administrative duties; and (h) \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Unit or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0have a PhD degree in an appropriate related discipline; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0have strong commitment to excellence in teaching and research; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0be able to demonstrate effective classroom teaching skills and have good interpersonal skills; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0have an excellent command of English; (e)\u00a0 \u00a0 have an excellent record of research and scholarship commensurate with their experience; and (f)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0demonstrate good potential in bidding for research grants as well as in establishing significant externally funded research programmes. The applicants should demonstrate strong potential to be internationally prominent through a track record of excellent research and teaching. They will be expected to contribute to the development and delivery of degree programmes; teach in engineering design relevant to their technical specialisation; and should have been involved in major research projects relevant to their discipline. Application is open to anyone with an outstanding research and teaching track record in the areas of Building Energy , Building Environment or Building Safety and Resilience . Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered. \u00a0Faculty members recruited through the Strategic Hiring Scheme at Chair Professor or Professor level will receive a start-up grant of HKD 5 million or more to support research activities (including the admission of two PhD students, purchase of equipment, hiring of research staff, etc.) in the initial five years, whereas those appointed at Associate Professor or Assistant Professor level will receive a start-up grant of HKD 3 million or more. Initial appointment for Assistant Professor will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.\u00a0 Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement.\u00a0\u00a0An appropriate term will be provided for appointment at Associate Professor level.\u00a0 For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . C onsideration of applications will commence on 22 June 2026 until the position is filled . Apply Now Posting date: 8 June 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260603011": {"title": "Part-time Visiting Lecturer (several posts)", "description": "Job Application - Part-time Visiting Lecturer  (several  posts) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification School of Optometry Part-time Visiting Lecturer  (several  posts) (Ref. 260603011) [Appointment period: tenable for 2026/2027 academic year] Duties The appointees will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0conduct teaching at undergraduate level in Optometry; and (b) \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of School or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have a doctoral degree in Optometry or an equivalent qualification and not less than three years of post-qualification teaching experience. Conditions of Service The remuneration rate is HK$900 per hour. Consideration of applications will commence on 17 June 2026 until the positions are filled. Apply Now Posting date: 3 June 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260603010": {"title": "Part-time Visiting Clinical Associate (several posts)", "description": "Job Application - Part-time Visiting Clinical Associate  (several  posts) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification School of Optometry Part-time Visiting Clinical Associate  (several  posts) (Ref. 260603010) [Appointment period: tenable for 2026/2027 academic year] Duties The appointees will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0teach and supervise optometry students in their clinical training; and (b) \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of School or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should: (c) \u00a0 \u00a0have a higher degree in Optometry or an equivalent qualification; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0have several years of relevant optometric experience; and (e) \u00a0 \u00a0be registered with the Optometrists Board of the HKSAR. Applicants possessing a bachelor\u2019s degree in Optometry with substantial relevant industry and optometric experience may also be considered. Conditions of Service The remuneration rate is from HK$525 per hour. Consideration of applications will commence on 17 June 2026 until the positions are filled. Apply Now Posting date: 3 June 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260601010": {"title": "Assistant Professor in Biomedical Engineering", "description": "Job Application - Assistant Professor in Biomedical Engineering Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Biomedical Engineering and Sports Technology Assistant Professor in Biomedical Engineering (Ref. 260601010) The Department of Biomedical Engineering (BME) is one of the five academic departments in the Faculty of Engineering, and it offers a full spectrum of BME programmes, from BSc, MSc to PhD. \u00a0The team is the first group to offer Biomedical Engineering related undergraduate programme in Hong Kong, and has made great achievements in BME education, innovative research, and technology transfer. \u00a0Currently BME has four thematic research areas, including Biomedical Imaging, Instrumentation, Sensing and AI, Molecular, Cellular and Tissue Engineering, Sports and Neuromusculoskeletal Engineering, Prosthetics, Orthotics, Smart Ageing and Rehabilitation Engineering. \u00a0It aims to conduct cutting-edge researches in these areas and nurture future leaders in prosthetics and orthotics, clinical engineering, medical instrumentation and sensors, and biological engineering by imparting interdisciplinary knowledge, innovative ideas, critical thinking and practical skills. \u00a0Please visit the website at http://www.polyu.edu.hk/bme for more information about the Unit. Duties The appointee will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0teach at undergraduate and postgraduate levels, and contribute to programme and curriculum development; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0initiate innovative research projects that leads to publications in top-tier refereed journals and awards of external research grants; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0supervise student projects and theses; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0engage in industrial and scholarly research/consultancy activities; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0undertake academic and departmental administrative duties; and (f) \u00a0 \u00a0 perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Unit or his delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0a PhD degree in Biomedical Engineering or Neurotechnology, with expertise in Biomedical Imaging or Brain Computer Interface or a related discipline; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0strong commitment to excellence in teaching and research; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0good publication records; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0good networking ability; and (e) \u00a0 \u00a0excellent communication skills and the ability to use English as the medium of instruction. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.\u00a0 Appointment will only be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract. Consideration of applications will commence on 15 June 2026 until the position is filled. Apply Now Posting date: 1 June 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260521007": {"title": "Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Microelectronics and Quantum Technology under Strategic Hiring Scheme (several posts)", "description": "Job Application - Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Microelectronics and Quantum Technology under Strategic Hiring Scheme  (several  posts) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Electrical and Electronic Engineering Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Microelectronics and Quantum Technology under Strategic Hiring Scheme  (several  posts) (Ref. 260521007) Since its inception in 1974, the Department of Electrical and Electronic Engineering (EEE), formed through the merger of the Department of Electronic and Information Engineering and the Department of Electrical Engineering, has maintained a distinguished history of providing outstanding engineering education and applied research in Hong Kong. The Unit offers extensive resources to support a wide variety of teaching activities and research interests, frequently hosting leading scholars for collaboration to enhance its global research profile. Please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/eee for more information about the Unit. EEE is a constituent unit in the Faculty of Engineering. Information on the Faculty is available at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/feng/ . To boost the leadership and impact of PolyU\u2019s research work in areas of significant societal needs and strategic importance, the Strategic Hiring Scheme is introduced to recruit faculty members at all levels and outstanding scholars are invited to join the University under the Strategic Hiring Scheme.\u00a0 Appointees recruited under the Strategic Hiring Scheme should have conducted / led world-leading research that is commensurate with the stage of their academic career. EEE is now seeking highly qualified candidates for Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor positions across several strategic research tracks. Duties (A) Microelectronics and Silicon Photonics Appointees for this track should possess substantial research experience in devices design, cleanroom fabrication and device characterization etc. EEE prioritizes expertise in device design, simulation, fabrication and packaging, specifically encouraging those with experience bridging microelectronics with silicon photonics or heterogeneous integration. Teaching Duties: The appointees will be responsible for delivering courses at both undergraduate and postgraduate levels specifically focused on silicon photonics and microelectronics. (B) Embedded Circuits and Packaging Appointees for this track should possess substantial research experience in advanced embedded circuits and electronic packaging technologies. EEE prioritizes expertise in embedded circuit design, simulation and system-level integration, specifically encouraging those with experience in SoC architectures, 2.5D/3D integration, chiplet packaging or co-packaged optics with FPGA. Teaching Duties: The appointees will be responsible for delivering courses at both undergraduate and postgraduate levels specifically focused on embedded circuit design and advanced packaging technologies. (C) Photonic Quantum Computing Appointees for this track should possess substantial research experience in quantum optics, integrated quantum photonics and photonic quantum computing experiments. EEE prioritizes expertise in quantum light sources and programmable photonic circuits, specifically encouraging those with experience in optical quantum information processing or hardware implementation of quantum algorithms. Teaching Duties: The appointees will be responsible for delivering courses at both undergraduate and postgraduate levels specifically focused on quantum optics, quantum computing, and quantum information processing. (D) Quantum Theory and Algorithms Appointees for this track should possess substantial research experience in quantum optics, photonic quantum computing theory, architectures and quantum error correction. EEE prioritizes expertise in developing architectures for scalable photonic quantum computers and designing quantum machine learning models, specifically encouraging those with experience in practical quantum applications or collaborating closely with experimental teams. Teaching Duties: The appointees will be responsible for delivering courses at both undergraduate and postgraduate levels specifically focused on quantum algorithms and quantum information theory. For all the above tracks, the appointees will also be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0undertake teaching duties at undergraduate and postgraduate levels in the area of Microelectronics, Photonics, Quantum Physics or Quantum Technology. Beyond these primary areas, the candidate should be prepared to contribute to multidisciplinary subjects across the EEE curriculum; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0conduct research that leads to publications in top-tier refereed journals; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0attract research fundings and support industrial researches; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0supervise student projects and theses; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0engage in scholarly research/consultancy in their area of expertise; (f)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0contribute to departmental services and activities; and (g) \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Unit or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0have a doctoral degree in a relevant discipline; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0have the relevant postdoctoral research experience and a publication record that is commensurate with the level of appointment; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0demonstrate excellence in original research and strong fundamental knowledge in one or more of the above-mentioned core research areas; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0demonstrate potential to establish significant externally funded research programmes; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0be able to demonstrate evidence of effective classroom teaching skills; and (f)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0have excellent communication skills and the ability to use English as the medium of instruction. Applicants for appointment at Professor or Associate Professor level should have a substantial number of years of experience and an excellent record of relevant academic and/or research achievement in the specified field. Applicants with less experience will be considered for appointment at the level of Assistant Professor. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered. \u00a0Faculty members recruited through the Strategic Hiring Scheme at Chair Professor or Professor level will receive a start-up grant of HKD 5 million or more to support research activities (including the admission of two PhD students, purchase of equipment, hiring of research staff, etc.) in the initial five years, whereas those appointed at Associate Professor or Assistant Professor level will receive a start-up grant of HKD 3 million or more. Initial appointment for Assistant Professor will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.\u00a0 Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement.\u00a0 An appropriate term will be provided for appointment at Professor / Associate Professor levels.\u00a0 For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . Consideration of applications will commence on 28 May 2026 until the positions are filled. Apply Now Posting date: 21 May 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260513001": {"title": "Job Application", "description": "Job Application - Joseph Needham Professorship in Science and Civilisation Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Faculty of Humanities Joseph Needham Professorship in Science and Civilisation (Ref. 260513001) The Faculty of Humanities at The Hong Kong Polytechnic University is dedicated to creating synergies among language, communication, history, culture, and technology in education and research, highlighting both the discovery and the transfer of knowledge. \u00a0It is a leading tertiary education provider in Asia in the fields of linguistics, language science, language technology, Chinese-English bilingual studies and translation, intercultural communication, professional communication, and cultural and historical studies of China. The Faculty also excels in areas such as AI and the humanities, computational linguistics, healthcare communication, language neuroscience, sociolinguistic studies, and speech therapy. \u00a0It consists of four academic units: Department of Chinese History and Culture, Department of English and Communication, Department of Language Science and Technology, and Division of Artificial Intelligence and the Humanities. \u00a0The appointee will be appointed as Chair Professor / Professor in one of the academic units under the Faculty of Humanities. \u00a0Please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/fh for more information about the Faculty. Duties The position calls for a visionary academic leader to advance the strategic and sustainable development of the Faculty in Science and Civilisation. The successful candidate will combine world-class scholarship with exceptional leadership to shape the future of these disciplines. The appointee will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0provide leadership in long-term strategic planning that aligns with the University\u2019s goals; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0provide leadership in strengthening local and international partnerships to advance research and education goals; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0develop scholarly initiatives by fostering collaboration, securing external funding, and enhancing innovative, high-impact interdisciplinary research; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0mentor junior faculty in teaching, research and service excellence; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0teach and develop curricula in science and civilisation, including Chinese science and technology history, at undergraduate and postgraduate levels; (f)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0supervise postgraduate students actively and provide guidance on their research and career development; (g) \u00a0 \u00a0provide active service to committee work at all levels in the Faculty and the University as well as to the scholarly community; (h) \u00a0 \u00a0provide administrative support and advice for academic and Faculty/department affairs; and (i)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Department or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0a PhD degree in a relevant discipline, evidence of eminent scholarship and substantial relevant experience in a senior academic position, and relevant professional qualifications where appropriate; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0a global perspective, proven track record of academic leadership, and a distinguished international reputation in research and scholarship; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0a strong record in attracting and managing competitive research funding; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0a strong potential to develop local and international networks of partnerships and linkages with the community, for both professional and public sectors; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0a strong commitment to excellence in teaching and learning with substantial relevant teaching experiences; (f)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0proven academic leadership and ability to foster collaboration with colleagues in teaching, intellectual contributions, and service activities to bring visibility, prestige and reputation to the University; and (g) \u00a0 \u00a0an excellent command of both English and Chinese. Applicants for appointment at the Chair Professor level should have attainment of an academic rank of full professor or above at an internationally reputable university. Applicants for appointment at the Professor level should have an excellent international reputation as a leading scholar. Applicants who have responded to the previous advertisement need not re-apply. Conditions of Service Terms of appointment and remuneration package are negotiable and highly competitive. For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . Application and Nomination The University invites applications and nominations for this appointment. \u00a0Please submit an application by clicking the \u201cApply Now\u201d button below. \u00a0Candidature may also be recommended by nominations via email to fh.search@polyu.edu.hk . \u00a0General information about the University is available at https://www.polyu.edu.hk or from the Human Resources Office [Tel: (852) 2766 5291]. Consideration of applications and nominations will commence on 1 July 2026 until the position is filled. Apply Now Posting date: 13 May 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260512006": {"title": "Instructor (English Language) (several posts)", "description": "Job Application - Instructor (English Language)  (several  posts) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Language Education Institute Instructor (English Language)  (several  posts) (Ref. 260512006) The Language Education Institute (LEI), a new academic unit established on 1 July 2025, formulates policies, designs curricula and delivers teaching activities for the education of languages among students at PolyU, focusing mainly on the Chinese and English languages. LEI strives to become a regional and international leader in language education, particularly in the application of the latest technologies in language learning, teaching and assessment.\u00a0 It drives scholarship and best practices in language education among the PolyU community. LEI comprises the Chinese Language Centre (CLC), English Language Centre (ELC) and Technology-Enhanced Language Education Centre (TELEC), which are constituent units with their own Directors. \u00a0CLC and ELC offer service language teaching in Chinese and English for all students in the University while TELEC undertakes service language teaching using digital learning platforms and technological tools such as artificial intelligence and immersive technologies. CLC and ELC are committed to excellence in learning and teaching and aim to strengthen students\u2019 language proficiency and communication skills, foster independent and life\u2011long learning, and support whole\u2011person development. \u00a0They provide English and Chinese language teaching services tailored to the diverse needs of the University\u2019s students, delivering language enhancement and communication subjects, including AI as a Tool for Language Learning, in accordance with University requirements. \u00a0In addition to curriculum\u2011based teaching, the Centres coordinate a range of co\u2011curricular learning activities to support students\u2019 academic development and learning needs.\u00a0 Please visit the websites at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/clc/ and https://www.polyu.edu.hk/elc/ respectively for more information about CLC and ELC. Duties The appointees will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0 teach a range of courses in English for Academic Purposes (EAP), English for Specific Purposes (ESP) and communication skills for students, with effective and responsible integration of AI/GenAI to enhance learning, teaching, and assessment; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0 engage in English language enhancement initiatives of the University, including workshops and support activities related to technology- and AI-enhanced language learning; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0 participate in the pedagogical development and administration of teaching and learning activities, including promoting student language skills through technology-enhanced language teaching methods and responsible AI use; and (d) \u00a0 \u00a0 perform any other duties as assigned by the Director of Language Education Institute or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0have a master\u2019s degree in English Language Education / TESOL / Applied Linguistics / Education or a related discipline; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0have a recognised language teaching qualification; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0preferably possess at least three years\u2019 post-qualification relevant teaching experience at tertiary level; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0have effective classroom teaching skills; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0have demonstrated strong commitment to excellence in teaching; (f)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0have demonstrated pedagogic AI competencies for English language education; and (g) \u00a0 \u00a0be a highly proficient English speaker. Preference will be given to teachers with experience or expertise in incorporating GenAI in language teaching, expertise in discipline-related English, digital literacies, assessment design, and supporting students to use AI tools for self-regulated language learning. Applicants should indicate in their cover letter how their qualifications and experience would enable them to effectively perform the duties of the post. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.\u00a0 Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.\u00a0 Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement. C onsideration of applications will commence on 1\u00a0June 2026 . Apply Now Posting date: 12 May 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260512005": {"title": "Teaching Fellow (English Language) (several posts)", "description": "Job Application - Teaching Fellow (English Language) (several  posts) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Language Education Institute Teaching Fellow (English Language) (several  posts) (Ref. 260512005) [will be conferred the title of Lecturer] The Language Education Institute (LEI), a new academic unit established on 1 July 2025, formulates policies, designs curricula and delivers teaching activities for the education of languages among students at PolyU, focusing mainly on the Chinese and English languages. LEI strives to become a regional and international leader in language education, particularly in the application of the latest technologies in language learning, teaching and assessment.\u00a0 It drives scholarship and best practices in language education among the PolyU community. LEI comprises the Chinese Language Centre (CLC), English Language Centre (ELC) and Technology-Enhanced Language Education Centre (TELEC), which are constituent units with their own Directors. \u00a0CLC and ELC offer service language teaching in Chinese and English for all students in the University while TELEC undertakes service language teaching using digital learning platforms and technological tools such as artificial intelligence and immersive technologies. CLC and ELC are committed to excellence in learning and teaching and aim to strengthen students\u2019 language proficiency and communication skills, foster independent and life\u2011long learning, and support whole\u2011person development. \u00a0They provide English and Chinese language teaching services tailored to the diverse needs of the University\u2019s students, delivering language enhancement and communication subjects, including AI as a Tool for Language Learning, in accordance with University requirements. \u00a0In addition to curriculum\u2011based teaching, the Centres coordinate a range of co\u2011curricular learning activities to support students\u2019 academic development and learning needs.\u00a0 Please visit the websites at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/clc/ and https://www.polyu.edu.hk/elc/ respectively for more information about CLC and ELC. Duties The appointees will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0teach a range of courses in English for Academic Purposes (EAP), English for Specific Purposes (ESP) and communication skills for students, with effective and responsible integration of AI/GenAI to enhance learning, teaching, and assessment; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0teach and lead curriculum development in English language education, including AI-integrated syllabus/assessment design and student guidance on responsible AI use; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0make a considerable contribution to the various aspects of the English Language Centre\u2019s work and digital initiatives through committee membership; and (d) \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Director of Language Education Institute or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0have a master\u2019s degree in English Language Education / TESOL / Applied Linguistics / Education or a related discipline; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0have a recognised language teaching qualification; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0possess at least four years\u2019 relevant post-qualification experience at tertiary level, with a good track record of teaching English in higher education; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0have experience in course and instructional design, including technology-enhanced learning; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0have demonstrated strong commitment to excellence in teaching; (f)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0have demonstrated pedagogic AI competencies for English language education; and (g) \u00a0 \u00a0be a highly proficient English speaker. Applicants should be active members within the discipline of language education as evidenced through participation in relevant conferences, the production of language teaching materials, and/or instructional design. \u00a0Applications are particularly welcome from teachers with expertise in EAP/academic literacy, multimodal communication, instructional and curriculum design, AI/GenAI-enhanced language pedagogy, or other areas of Applied Linguistics if of direct relevance to Language Education. Applicants should indicate in their cover letter how their qualifications and experience would enable them to effectively perform the duties of the post. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.\u00a0 Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.\u00a0 Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement. C onsideration of applications will commence on 1\u00a0June 2026 . Apply Now Posting date: 12 May 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260512004": {"title": "Senior Teaching Fellow (English Language) (several posts)", "description": "Job Application - Senior Teaching Fellow (English Language) (several posts) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Language Education Institute Senior Teaching Fellow (English Language) (several posts) (Ref. 260512004) [will be conferred the title of Senior Lecturer] The Language Education Institute (LEI), a new academic unit established on 1 July 2025, formulates policies, designs curricula and delivers teaching activities for the education of languages among students at PolyU, focusing mainly on the Chinese and English languages. LEI strives to become a regional and international leader in language education, particularly in the application of the latest technologies in language learning, teaching and assessment.\u00a0 It drives scholarship and best practices in language education among the PolyU community. LEI comprises the Chinese Language Centre (CLC), English Language Centre (ELC) and Technology-Enhanced Language Education Centre (TELEC), which are constituent units with their own Directors. \u00a0CLC and ELC offer service language teaching in Chinese and English for all students in the University while TELEC undertakes service language teaching using digital learning platforms and technological tools such as artificial intelligence and immersive technologies. CLC and ELC are committed to excellence in learning and teaching and aim to strengthen students\u2019 language proficiency and communication skills, foster independent and life\u2011long learning, and support whole\u2011person development. \u00a0They provide English and Chinese language teaching services tailored to the diverse needs of the University\u2019s students, delivering language enhancement and communication subjects, including AI as a Tool for Language Learning, in accordance with University requirements. \u00a0In addition to curriculum\u2011based teaching, the Centres coordinate a range of co\u2011curricular learning activities to support students\u2019 academic development and learning needs.\u00a0 Please visit the websites at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/clc/ and https://www.polyu.edu.hk/elc/ respectively for more information about CLC and ELC. Duties The appointees will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0teach a range of courses in English for Academic Purposes (EAP), English for Specific Purposes (ESP) and communication skills for students, with effective and responsible integration of AI/GenAI to enhance learning, teaching, and assessment; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0provide effective and visionary leadership in a position of responsibility as coordinator of at least one major aspect of the English Language Centre\u2019s operation, including (where appropriate) leadership in AI-integrated curriculum, assessment and responsible-use practices; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0make a considerable contribution to the various aspects of the Centre\u2019s work and digital initiatives through committee membership; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0play a leading administrative and pedagogic role in the Centre\u2019s operation, including mentoring colleagues in AI-enhanced language teaching and the development of student AI literacy; and (e)\u00a0 \u00a0 perform any other duties as assigned by the Director of Language Education Institute or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0a master\u2019s degree in English Language Education / TESOL / Applied Linguistics / Education or a related discipline, and preferably a PhD in a relevant field; (b)\u00a0 \u00a0 a recognised language teaching qualification; (c)\u00a0 \u00a0 at least nine years\u2019 post-master\u2019s or at least six years\u2019 post-doctoral relevant teaching experience at tertiary level, with a strong track record of teaching English in higher education; (d)\u00a0 \u00a0 considerable experience of, and demonstrated competence in, the coordination and management of teaching and learning activity at tertiary level, including curriculum leadership and quality assurance; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0demonstrated strong commitment to excellence in teaching; (f)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0demonstrated pedagogic AI competencies for English language education; and (g) \u00a0 \u00a0a high proficiency in spoken and written English. Applicants should demonstrate active scholarly engagement in the field of language education, through activities such as leading teaching-related projects, delivering presentations and publishing research at relevant conferences, developing language teaching materials, and/or undertaking instructional design work. \u00a0Applications are particularly welcome from teachers with expertise in EAP/academic literacy, multimodal communication, instructional and curriculum design, AI/GenAI-enhanced language pedagogy, or other areas of Applied Linguistics if of direct relevance to Language Education. Applicants should indicate in their cover letter how their qualifications and experience would enable them to effectively perform the duties of the post. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.\u00a0 Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.\u00a0 Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement. C onsideration of applications will commence on 1\u00a0June 2026. Apply Now Posting date: 12 May 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260512003": {"title": "Instructor (Chinese Language) (several posts)", "description": "Job Application - Instructor (Chinese Language) (several posts) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Language Education Institute Instructor (Chinese Language) (several posts) (Ref. 260512003) The Language Education Institute (LEI), a new academic unit established on 1 July 2025, formulates policies, designs curricula and delivers teaching activities for the education of languages among students at PolyU, focusing mainly on the Chinese and English languages. LEI strives to become a regional and international leader in language education, particularly in the application of the latest technologies in language learning, teaching and assessment. \u00a0It drives scholarship and best practices in language education among the PolyU community. LEI comprises the Chinese Language Centre (CLC), English Language Centre (ELC) and Technology-Enhanced Language Education Centre (TELEC), which are constituent units with their own Directors. \u00a0CLC and ELC offer service language teaching in Chinese and English for all students in the University while TELEC undertakes service language teaching using digital learning platforms and technological tools such as artificial intelligence and immersive technologies. CLC and ELC are committed to excellence in learning and teaching and aim to strengthen students\u2019 language proficiency and communication skills, foster independent and life\u2011long learning, and support whole\u2011person development. \u00a0They provide Chinese and English language teaching services tailored to the diverse needs of the University\u2019s students, delivering language enhancement and communication subjects, including AI as a Tool for Language Learning, in accordance with University requirements. \u00a0In addition to curriculum\u2011based teaching, the Centres coordinate a range of co\u2011curricular learning activities to support students\u2019 academic development and learning needs.\u00a0 Please visit the websites at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/clc/ and https://www.polyu.edu.hk/elc/ respectively for more information about CLC and ELC. Duties The appointees will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0teach a range of courses in Chinese for Academic Purposes (CAP), Chinese for Specific Purposes (CSP) and communication skills for undergraduate students, with effective and responsible integration of AI/GenAI to enhance learning, teaching, and assessment; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0engage in Chinese language enhancement initiatives of the University, including workshops and support activities related to technology- and AI-enhanced language learning; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0participate in the pedagogical development and administration of teaching and learning activities, including promoting student language skills through technology-enhanced language teaching methods and responsible AI use; and (d) \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Director of Language Education Institute or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0a master\u2019s degree in Applied Linguistics / Chinese Language/Literature / Chinese Language Education or a related discipline; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0preferably at least three years\u2019 post-qualification relevant teaching experience at tertiary level; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0effective classroom teaching skills; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0demonstrated strong commitment to excellence in teaching; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0demonstrated pedagogic AI competencies for Chinese language education; (f)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0an excellent command of written Chinese with proficiency in Putonghua (at least B2 level in Putonghua Shuiping Ceshi [PSC] or equivalent) and Cantonese; and (g) \u00a0 \u00a0the ability to use English as a working language. Preference will be given to teachers with experience or expertise in incorporating GenAI in language teaching, expertise in discipline-related Chinese, digital literacies, assessment design, and supporting students to use AI tools for self-regulated language learning. Preference may be given to those with relevant teaching experience in Chinese/Putonghua at tertiary level, including subjects offered to non-Chinese speaking students. Applicants should indicate in their cover letter how their qualifications and experience would enable them to effectively perform the duties of the post. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.\u00a0 Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.\u00a0 Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement. Consideration of applications will commence on 1\u00a0June 2026 . Apply Now Posting date: 12 May 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260512002": {"title": "Teaching Fellow (Chinese Language) (several posts)", "description": "Job Application - Teaching Fellow (Chinese Language) (several  posts) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Language Education Institute Teaching Fellow (Chinese Language) (several  posts) (Ref. 260512002) [will be conferred the title of Lecturer] The Language Education Institute (LEI), a new academic unit established on 1 July 2025, formulates policies, designs curricula and delivers teaching activities for the education of languages among students at PolyU, focusing mainly on the Chinese and English languages. LEI strives to become a regional and international leader in language education, particularly in the application of the latest technologies in language learning, teaching and assessment. \u00a0It drives scholarship and best practices in language education among the PolyU community. LEI comprises the Chinese Language Centre (CLC), English Language Centre (ELC) and Technology-Enhanced Language Education Centre (TELEC), which are constituent units with their own Directors.\u00a0 CLC and ELC offer service language teaching in Chinese and English for all students in the University while TELEC undertakes service language teaching using digital learning platforms and technological tools such as artificial intelligence and immersive technologies. CLC and ELC are committed to excellence in learning and teaching and aim to strengthen students\u2019 language proficiency and communication skills, foster independent and life\u2011long learning, and support whole\u2011person development. \u00a0They provide Chinese and English language teaching services tailored to the diverse needs of the University\u2019s students, delivering language enhancement and communication subjects, including AI as a Tool for Language Learning, in accordance with University requirements. \u00a0In addition to curriculum\u2011based teaching, the Centres coordinate a range of co\u2011curricular learning activities to support students\u2019 academic development and learning needs.\u00a0 Please visit the websites at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/clc/ and https://www.polyu.edu.hk/elc/ respectively for more information about CLC and ELC. Duties The appointees will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0teach a range of courses in Chinese for Academic Purposes (CAP), Chinese for Specific Purposes (CSP) and communication skills for students, with effective and responsible integration of AI/GenAI to enhance learning, teaching, and assessment; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0teach and lead curriculum development in Chinese language education, including AI-integrated syllabus/assessment design and student guidance on responsible AI use; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0make a considerable contribution to the various aspects of the Chinese Language Centre\u2019s work and digital initiatives through committee membership; and (d) \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Director of Language Education Institute or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0a master\u2019s degree in Applied Linguistics / Chinese Language/Literature / Language Education or a related discipline; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0at least four years\u2019 relevant post-qualification experience at tertiary level, with a good track record of teaching Chinese in higher education; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0experience in course and instructional design, including technology-enhanced learning; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0demonstrated strong commitment to excellence in teaching; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0demonstrated pedagogic AI competencies for Chinese language education; (f)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0an excellent command of written Chinese with proficiency in Putonghua (at least B2 level in Putonghua Shuiping Ceshi [PSC] or equivalent) and Cantonese; and (g) \u00a0 \u00a0the ability to use English as a working language. Applicants should be active members within the discipline of language education as evidenced through participation in relevant conferences, the production of language teaching materials, and/or instructional design. \u00a0Applications are particularly welcome from teachers with expertise in Chinese for Academic Purpose/academic literacy, multimodal communication, instructional and curriculum design, AI/GenAI-enhanced language pedagogy, or other areas of Applied Linguistics if of direct relevance to Language Education. Applicants should indicate in their cover letter how their qualifications and experience would enable them to effectively perform the duties of the post. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.\u00a0 Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.\u00a0 Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement. C onsideration of applications will commence on 1\u00a0June 2026. Apply Now Posting date: 12 May 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260512001": {"title": "Senior Teaching Fellow (Chinese Language) (several posts)", "description": "Job Application - Senior Teaching Fellow (Chinese Language) (several  posts) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Language Education Institute Senior Teaching Fellow (Chinese Language) (several  posts) (Ref. 260512001) [will be conferred the title of Senior Lecturer] The Language Education Institute (LEI), a new academic unit established on 1 July 2025, formulates policies, designs curricula and delivers teaching activities for the education of languages among students at PolyU, focusing mainly on the Chinese and English languages. LEI strives to become a regional and international leader in language education, particularly in the application of the latest technologies in language learning, teaching and assessment. \u00a0It drives scholarship and best practices in language education among the PolyU community. LEI comprises the Chinese Language Centre (CLC), English Language Centre (ELC) and Technology-Enhanced Language Education Centre (TELEC), which are constituent units with their own Directors.\u00a0 CLC and ELC offer service language teaching in Chinese and English for all students in the University while TELEC undertakes service language teaching using digital learning platforms and technological tools such as artificial intelligence and immersive technologies. CLC and ELC are committed to excellence in learning and teaching and aim to strengthen students\u2019 language proficiency and communication skills, foster independent and life\u2011long learning, and support whole\u2011person development. \u00a0They provide Chinese and English language teaching services tailored to the diverse needs of the University\u2019s students, delivering language enhancement and communication subjects, including AI as a Tool for Language Learning, in accordance with University requirements. \u00a0In addition to curriculum\u2011based teaching, the Centres coordinate a range of co\u2011curricular learning activities to support students\u2019 academic development and learning needs.\u00a0 Please visit the websites at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/clc/ and https://www.polyu.edu.hk/elc/ respectively for more information about CLC and ELC. Duties The appointees will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0teach a range of courses in Chinese for Academic Purposes (CAP), Chinese for Specific Purposes (CSP) and communication skills for students, with effective and responsible integration of AI/GenAI to enhance learning, teaching, and assessment; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0provide effective and visionary leadership in a position of responsibility as coordinator of at least one major aspect of the Chinese Language Centre\u2019s operation, including (where appropriate) leadership in AI-integrated curriculum, assessment and responsible-use practices; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0make a considerable contribution to the various aspects of the Centre\u2019s work and digital initiatives through committee membership; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0play a leading administrative and pedagogic role in the Centre\u2019s operation, including mentoring colleagues in AI-enhanced language teaching and the development of student AI literacy; and (e) \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Director of Language Education Institute or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0a master\u2019s degree in Applied Linguistics / Chinese Language/Literature / Language Education or a related discipline, and preferably a PhD in a relevant field; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0at least nine years\u2019 post-Master\u2019s or at least six years\u2019 post-doctoral relevant teaching experience at tertiary level, with a strong track record of teaching Chinese in higher education; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0considerable experience of, and demonstrated competence in, the coordination and management of teaching and learning activities at tertiary level, including curriculum leadership and quality assurance; (d)\u00a0 \u00a0 demonstrated strong commitment to excellence in teaching; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0demonstrated pedagogic AI competencies for Chinese language education; and (f)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0the ability to use English as a working language. Applicants should demonstrate active scholarly engagement in the field of language education, through activities such as leading teaching-related projects, delivering presentations and publishing research at relevant conferences, developing language teaching materials, and/or undertaking instructional design work. \u00a0Applications are particularly welcome from teachers with expertise in Chinese for Academic Purpose/academic literacy, multimodal communication, instructional and curriculum design, AI/GenAI-enhanced language pedagogy, or other areas of Applied Linguistics if of direct relevance to Language Education. Applicants should indicate in their cover letter how their qualifications and experience would enable them to effectively perform the duties of the post. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.\u00a0 Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.\u00a0 Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement. C onsideration of applications will commence on 1\u00a0June 2026. Apply Now Posting date: 12 May 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260505010": {"title": "Clinical Associate (two posts)", "description": "Job Application - Clinical Associate (two posts) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification School of Nursing Clinical Associate (two posts) (Ref. 260505010) [will be conferred the title of Assistant Professor of Practice] Established in 1977, the School of Nursing supports the mission of the University by nurturing graduates who are critical thinkers, effective communicators, innovative problem solvers, lifelong learners and ethical leaders. \u00a0It ranks 18th for the best School of Nursing internationally (QS Ranking 2026). \u00a0The education, research, consultancy and integrative health services are driven by a commitment to improve health of the community. \u00a0Currently, it has a total of around 80 full-time faculty members. \u00a0We welcome candidates from all nursing disciplines, including critical care, mental health, as well as prevention and infection control. Duties The appointees will be required to: (a) perform classroom teaching and clinical supervision duties in nursing and related areas; (b) teach pre-registration nursing programmes and supervise students in clinical/field studies; (c) supervise clinical projects and clinical practicum at undergraduate and postgraduate levels; (d) contribute to curriculum development and quality improvement of clinical studies; (e) act as student advisor and counsellor; (f)\u00a0 coordinate student clinical placement with local, national and overseas healthcare agencies; and (g) perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of School or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) a relevant master\u2019s degree plus not less than four years of post-qualification/post-registration clinical experience in nursing or related areas; (b) a Certificate of Registration (Part I and/or II) issued by The Nursing Board/Council of Hong Kong; (c) a valid practicing certificate issued by The Nursing Council of Hong Kong; (d) a solid track record as a nursing educator with demonstrated experience in both hands-on clinical supervision and classroom teaching; (e) significant contribution to educational innovations and quality improvement initiatives across both clinical practicum and academic settings; (f) demonstrated potential for making substantial contributions to curriculum and pedagogy development and programme management; (g) a good command of both written and spoken English and Chinese, with fluency in Cantonese; and (h) effective pedagogical skills across various delivery formats, including classroom teaching and direct clinical supervision, coupled with good interpersonal and communication skills. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.\u00a0 Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.\u00a0 Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement. Consideration of applications will commence on 19 May 2026 until the positions are filled. Apply Now Posting date: 5 May 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260427004": {"title": "Teaching Fellow in Shipping, Maritime and Transport Studies", "description": "Job Application - Teaching Fellow in Shipping, Maritime and Transport Studies Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Logistics and Maritime Studies Teaching Fellow in Shipping, Maritime and Transport Studies (Ref. 260427004) [will be conferred the title of Lecturer] Duties The appointee will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0engage in teaching Logistics and Maritime Studies subjects and undertake related pedagogical activities at undergraduate and postgraduate levels; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0contribute to programme/curriculum design, development and administration, and engage actively in scholarly activities; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0provide support for academic and departmental affairs; and (d) \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of the Unit or his delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0a doctoral degree in a relevant discipline plus not less than three years of post-qualification tertiary teaching experience; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0good subject knowledge, skills and competence in the appropriate academic or professional discipline; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0strong commitment to excellence in teaching; and (d) \u00a0 \u00a0an excellent command of English and good communication skills. Preference will be given to those with relevant teaching experience in tertiary institutions. Applicants who have responded to the previous advertisement(s) need not re-apply. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.\u00a0 Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.\u00a0 Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement. Consideration of applications will commence on 11 June 2026 until the position is filled . Apply Now Posting date: 4 June 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260424016": {"title": "Teaching Fellow (Temporary Appointment) (three posts)", "description": "Job Application - Teaching Fellow (Temporary Appointment)  (three posts) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Computing Teaching Fellow (Temporary Appointment)  (three posts) (Ref. 260424016) [Appointment period: each for twelve months initially, with possibility of further appointment] Duties The appointees will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0undertake teaching duties at both undergraduate and postgraduate levels, including the coordination and supervision of student seminars, tutorials and projects/theses; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0engage in teaching, learning and scholarly activities; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0contribute to the planning, administration and development of programmes/courses; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0assist in organising student activities/training workshops to promote students\u2019 learning experience; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0undertake administrative duties in academic and departmental affairs; and (f)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Unit or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0a PhD degree in Computer Science, Information Technology or related disciplines; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0at least three years of post-qualification tertiary teaching experience and/or relevant professional, practical, or industrial experience; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0good subject knowledge, skills and competence in the discipline; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0effective classroom teaching skills and a strong commitment to excellence in teaching and professional service; and (e) \u00a0 \u00a0an excellent command of both written and spoken English, good communication and interpersonal skills. Applicants should also submit (i) an updated curriculum vitae; and (ii) a teaching statement elaborating his/her teaching philosophy and contribution for the position applied. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered. C onsideration of applications will commence on 15 May 2026 until the positions are filled . Apply Now Posting date: 24 April 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260421011": {"title": "Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Management", "description": "Job Application - Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Management Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Management and Marketing Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Management (Ref. 260421011) The Department of Management and Marketing (MM) is one of the constituent departments of the Faculty of Business. According to the 2025 US News and World Report Global University Ranking, PolyU is ranked 58 th in the Best Global Universities and 25 th in the Best Universities for Economics and Business (7 th in Asia). The University of Texas at Dallas ranks our faculty's research 38 th in the world and 5 th in Asia (as of March 2026). MM currently has around 60 full-time academic staff who are dedicated to providing cutting-edge knowledge and practical skills for our students in three key areas of business \u2014 Management , Marketing , and Management Information Systems . We offer a full range of programmes leading to the awards of Doctor of Philosophy, Master of Science, and Bachelor of Business Administration. Our doctoral program has successfully placed our PhD students in elite institutions in Asia and Australia, including Hong Kong University of Science & Technology, City University of Hong Kong, Renmin University, and Deakin University. The Management discipline of the Department invites applications for open-ranked faculty positions in the Organisational Behavior and Human Resources\u00a0(OBHR)\u00a0and Strategic Management areas . The faculty members in the Management discipline of MM regularly publish their research in top-tier journals such as the Academy of Management Journal , Journal of Applied Psychology , Strategic Management Journal , Organization Science , Journal of International Business Studies , and other premier outlets. Our research support includes a reduced teaching load in the first three years, generous start-up grant, and considerate administrative services for junior members. The department has a collegial environment. Currently the OBHR team includes Wu Liu, Michael Bond, Krishna Savani, Yi (Amy) Ou, Jia (Katrina) Lin, Jun (Melody) Zhang, Ren Li, Mannok Wong, Zhishuang (Olivia) Guan, Jingfeng Yin, and Kun Wang; the Strategic Management team includes Chinien Chung, Shuping Li, Xueyong Zhan, Qi Zhu, Hangjun Cho, Junghyun Mah, and Qinyu (Ryan) Wang. Please visit the website at https://mm.polyu.edu.hk/ for more information about MM.\u00a0 Applicants are invited to contact Professor Wu Liu, Professor of Department of Management and Marketing by email at wu.liu@polyu.edu.hk or Professor Chinien Chung, Associate Dean and Chair Professor of Strategic and Organization Management by email at chinien.chung@polyu.edu.hk for further information about the post. Duties The appointee will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0engage in top-level scholarly research in their areas of expertise; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0supervise research students; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0secure external competitive research grants; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0teach at the undergraduate and/or postgraduate levels; and (e) \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Unit or his delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0a PhD degree in Management or a relevant discipline at the time of appointment or be close to receiving it; and (b) \u00a0 \u00a0a focused research orientation and the potential or demonstrated ability to publish in high quality scholarly journals. Conditions of Service The compensation package, teaching loads, and research support are highly competitive. \u00a0Initial appointment for Assistant Professor will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.\u00a0 Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement.\u00a0\u00a0An appropriate term will be provided for appointment at\u00a0Associate Professor / Professor levels.\u00a0 For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . C onsideration of applications will commence on 2 July 2026 until the position is filled . Apply Now Posting date: 24 June 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260421008": {"title": "Teaching Fellow", "description": "Job Application - Teaching Fellow Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification School of Design Teaching Fellow (Ref. 260421008) [will be conferred the title of Lecturer] Duties The appointee will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0develop subjects for the Social Design programme that synthesises knowledge and design applications with theories, design research methods and form-giving techniques; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0teach at the undergraduate level across all levels of the undergraduate Bachelor of Arts (BA) Design programme and across core and elective studio, seminar and lecture subjects, with adjustment in the teaching delivery to correspond to the subject; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0work closely with the programme coordinator and faculty members to facilitate the execution of the programme and offer support in various administrative and educational tasks, academic activities and service which may span design disciplines; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0support the preparation and coordination of the admission exercise for the Social and Service Design programme, which may include reviewing applications, conducting interviews, and evaluating portfolios; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0act as an academic advisor and provide student support across all student levels as needed with intensive supervisory support provided to final year students completing their final year project; (f) \u00a0 \u00a0collaborate with the academic team to ensure curriculum alignment with industry standards and emerging trends in social and service design, community engagement, and sustainable practices, with a view to programme relevance and institutional influence; (g) \u00a0 \u00a0provide insights and expertise in social design methodologies, community engagement strategies, and sustainable development to enhance programme content quality and relevance; (h) \u00a0 \u00a0engage with prospective students to provide information about the programme, answer inquiries, and assist in the admission process; (i)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0contribute to the planning and execution of promotional events and activities related to the launch and continuing reputation of the Social and Service Design programme; (j)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0actively seek out inter-departmental collaborative teaching opportunities that promote the BA Design Scheme as a whole; and (k)\u00a0 \u00a0 perform any other duties as assigned by the Dean of School or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0have a master\u2019s degree in disciplines related to social design, service design, community development, or related fields, with not less than three years of post-qualification experience in tertiary teaching and/or professional practice within the social and service design industry; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0demonstrate expertise and proficiency in: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0procedural workflows in social and service design and utilisation of tools for designing interventions; \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0community engagement strategies, including working with diverse communities and advocating for marginalised populations; and \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0curriculum development tailored to the unique requirements of social and service design education; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0showcase the ability to conduct tutorials, workshops and assessments within the domain of social and service design; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0possess exceptional oral and written communication skills to effectively engage with individuals from diverse backgrounds; and (e) \u00a0 \u00a0be strongly committed to excellence in teaching and learning. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered. \u00a0Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract. \u00a0Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement. Consideration of applications will commence on 28 April 2026 until the position is filled. Apply Now Posting date: 21 April 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260415007": {"title": "Teaching Fellow in Supply Chain and Operations Management (two posts)", "description": "Job Application - Teaching Fellow in Supply Chain and Operations Management  (two posts) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Logistics and Maritime Studies Teaching Fellow in Supply Chain and Operations Management  (two posts) (Ref. 260415007) [will be conferred the title of Lecturer] Duties The appointees will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0engage in teaching Supply Chain Management, Logistics, Operations and Quality Management related subjects and undertake related pedagogical activities at undergraduate and postgraduate levels; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0contribute to programme/curriculum design, development and administration, and engage actively in scholarly activities; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0provide support for academic and departmental affairs; and (d) \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of the Unit or his delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0a doctoral degree in a relevant discipline plus not less than three years of post-qualification tertiary teaching experience; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0good subject knowledge, skills and competence in the appropriate academic or professional discipline; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0strong commitment to excellence in teaching; and (d) \u00a0 \u00a0an excellent command of English and good communication skills. Preference will be given to those with relevant teaching experience in tertiary institutions. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.\u00a0 Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.\u00a0 Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement. C onsideration of applications will commence on 22 April 2026 until the positions are filled . Apply Now Posting date: 15 April 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260311019": {"title": "Chair Professor / Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Food Safety / Future Food Technology / Food Materials / Microbiomes and Health / Functional Food under Strategic Hiring Scheme", "description": "Job Application - Chair Professor / Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Food Safety / Future Food Technology / Food Materials / Microbiomes and Health / Functional Food under Strategic Hiring Scheme Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Food Science and Nutrition Chair Professor / Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Food Safety / Future Food Technology / Food Materials / Microbiomes and Health / Functional Food under Strategic Hiring Scheme (Ref. 260311019) The Department of Food Science and Nutrition is a multi-disciplinary department established from 1 January 2023 under the Faculty of Science. \u00a0With the unique standing in Hong Kong and the commitment to quality teaching, research excellence and knowledge transfer, the Department is envisioned to develop all-rounded graduates with professional qualifications, and promote interdisciplinary research with positive societal impacts.\u00a0 The Department\u2019s key research pillars are Food Safety, Food Technology, Human Nutrition and Chinese Medicine.\u00a0 Currently, there are about 21 academic and teaching staff and 13 Research Assistant Professors in the Department. \u00a0Please visit the website at http:// www.polyu.edu.hk/fsn/ for more information about the Department. The Hong Kong Special Administrative Region is an international city located strategically at the heart of Asia and is the gateway to the Chinese Mainland, with excellent transport links to major international cities. The Department is seeking highly motivated and suitably qualified individuals with research expertise in Food Safety / Future Food Technology / Food Materials / Microbiomes and Health / Functional Food. To boost the leadership and impact of PolyU\u2019s research work in areas of significant societal needs and strategic importance, the Strategic Hiring Scheme is introduced to recruit faculty members at all levels and outstanding scholars are invited to join the University under the Strategic Hiring Scheme.\u00a0 Appointees recruited under the Strategic Hiring Scheme should have conducted / led world-leading research that is commensurate with the stage of their academic career. Duties The appointees will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0teach at undergraduate and postgraduate levels in related disciplines; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0conduct impactful research that leads to publications in high-quality refereed journals and external grants, generates meaningful societal impact, and addresses pressing real-world challenges; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0undertake research, programme/curriculum development and administration; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0supervise student projects at undergraduate and postgraduate levels; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0engage in industrial and scholarly research/consultancy activities; (f)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0undertake academic and departmental administrative duties; and (g) \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Department or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0a PhD degree in Food Science / Technology / Safety and Nutrition or a related field; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0a strong commitment to excellence in teaching and research, with demonstrated experience in the application of innovative approaches, including but not limited to advancements in food science, technology, safety or nutrition; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0strong records of high-quality research, publications and scholarship in Food Science / Technology / Safety and Nutrition or related areas; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0good networking ability and excellent potential to become a world-leading scholar; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0excellent communication skills and the ability to use English as the medium of instruction; and (f)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0strong interdisciplinary research vision that promotes collaboration and synergy with our existing faculty. Applicants for appointment at the Chair Professor level should have an outstanding record of global leadership and research achievement in the community, in addition to substantial years of relevant post-qualification experience. Applicants for appointment at the Professor or Associate Professor level should have a substantial number of years of experience and an excellent record of relevant academic and/or research achievement in the specified field. \u00a0Applicants with less experience will be considered for appointment at the level of Assistant Professor. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered. \u00a0Faculty members recruited through the Strategic Hiring Scheme at Chair Professor or Professor level will receive a start-up grant of HKD 5 million or more to support research activities (including the admission of two PhD students, purchase of equipment, hiring of research staff, etc.) in the initial five years, whereas those appointed at Associate Professor or Assistant Professor level will receive a start-up grant of HKD 3 million or more. Initial appointment for Assistant Professor will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract. \u00a0Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement. \u00a0An appropriate term will be provided for appointment at Associate Professor / Professor / Chair Professor levels. \u00a0For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . Consideration of applications will commence on 25 March 2026 until the positions are filled . Apply Now Posting date: 11 March 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260127005": {"title": "Chair Professor / Professor in Urban Safety and Health under Strategic Hiring Scheme", "description": "Job Application - Chair Professor / Professor in Urban Safety and Health under Strategic Hiring Scheme Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Faculty of Construction and Environment Chair Professor / Professor in Urban Safety and Health under Strategic Hiring Scheme (Ref. 260127005) The Faculty of Construction and Environment (FCE) has the largest concentration of expertise in Hong Kong in construction and environment-related disciplines. Organised into the Department of Architecture*, the Department of Building Environment and Energy Engineering, the Department of Building and Real Estate, the Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering, and the Department of Land Surveying and Geo-Informatics, the Faculty is in a unique position to take advantage of its prime location to play a leading role in sustainable urbanisation as well as smart city development in the region and beyond. The Faculty is inviting applications for the position of Chair Professor / Professor in Urban Safety and Health. The appointee, affiliating with one of the academic units of the Faculty, will be expected to provide world-leading academic leadership, drive innovative and high-impact research and deliver high-quality education in the field. *The Department of Architecture is a new academic unit under FCE to be established with effect from 1 July 2026. Duties The appointee will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0provide leadership in long-term strategic planning that aligns with the University and the Faculty\u2019s strategic goals, with specific focus on enhancing research impact in the area of urban safety and health; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0provide leadership in strengthening local and international partnerships with academia, industry partners, government agencies and professional bodies to advance research and education goals; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0initiate, lead and conduct world-leading research, through fostering interdisciplinary collaboration, developing innovative and high-impact research, securing substantial external competitive research funding, and publishing quality outputs in top-tier international journals; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0provide mentorship to junior faculty leading to teaching, research and service excellence; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0undertake teaching duties at undergraduate and postgraduate levels, including curriculum design and development; (f) \u00a0 \u00a0supervise postgraduate students actively and provide guidance on their research and career development; (g) \u00a0 \u00a0provide active service to committee work at all levels in the Faculty and the University as well as to the scholarly and professional community; (h) \u00a0 \u00a0provide administrative support and advice for academic and Faculty/Department affairs; and (i)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Unit or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0a PhD degree in a relevant discipline, such as Fire Safety Engineering, Civil / Structural Engineering, or Construction Management, coupled with evidence of eminent scholarship and substantial relevant experience in a senior academic position, and relevant professional qualifications where appropriate; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0attainment of an academic rank of full professor or above at an internationally reputable university; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0a global perspective, a proven track record of academic leadership, and a distinguished international reputation in research and scholarship; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0a strong record in attracting and managing competitive research funding; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0proven ability to develop local and international networks of partnerships and linkages with the community, for both professional and public sectors; and (f) \u00a0 \u00a0a strong commitment to excellence in teaching and learning with substantial relevant teaching experiences. Applicants for appointment at the Chair Professor level should demonstrate an outstanding level of scholarly accomplishments, with international reputation as one of the most distinguished scholars globally; and proven academic leadership and ability to foster collaboration with colleagues in teaching, intellectual contributions and service activities to bring more visibility, prestige and reputation to the University. Applicants for appointment at the Professor level should have a high degree of proficiency in teaching and research, significant impact in the field of specialisation, and an excellent international reputation as a leading scholar. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered. \u00a0Faculty members recruited through the Strategic Hiring Scheme at Chair Professor or Professor level will receive a start-up grant of HKD 5 million or more to support research activities (including the admission of two PhD students, purchase of equipment, hiring of research staff, etc.) in the initial five years, whereas those appointed at Associate Professor or Assistant Professor level will receive a start-up grant of HKD 3 million or more.\u00a0\u00a0For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . Consideration of applications will commence on 23 February 2026 until the position is filled. Apply Now Posting date: 27 January 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=251111014": {"title": "Global Search for Chair Professor / Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Architecture", "description": "Job Application - Global Search for Chair Professor / Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Architecture Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Architecture Global Search for Chair Professor / Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Architecture (Ref. 251111014) The Hong Kong Polytechnic University (PolyU) is inviting outstanding scholars to join our newly established Department of Architecture (ARCH) as Chair Professors, Professors, Associate Professors and Assistant Professors. PolyU is going to establish the Department of Architecture under the Faculty of Construction and Environment (FCE) with effect from 1 July 2026. \u00a0FCE is globally renowned for its excellence in Architecture & Built Environment and Civil & Structural Engineering, both ranked 17 th worldwide by Quacquarelli Symonds (QS Subject Ranking) in 2025. As a new dynamic hub for architectural innovation, the Department aims to consolidate FCE\u2019s academic strengths, drive innovative education and research, attract global talent, and elevate both the Faculty\u2019s and PolyU\u2019s international standing in architecture and advanced technologies. The Department is looking for enthusiastic and established outstanding scholars to join the team and help build a strong academic community to achieve transformative impact in AI-enhanced and big data driven architectural education and research. Our priority research areas include: \u2022 \u00a0 Architecture Technology and Engineering \u2022\u00a0 \u00a0Architecture & Digital Theory \u2022\u00a0 \u00a0Urban Planning and Design \u2022 \u00a0 Urban Analytics & Smart Cities \u2022\u00a0 \u00a0Sustainable Architecture Design Technology \u2022\u00a0 \u00a0Landscape Architecture \u2022\u00a0 \u00a0Heritage Conservation / Architectural Heritage To boost the leadership and impact of PolyU\u2019s research work in areas of significant societal needs and strategic importance, the Strategic Hiring Scheme (SHS) has been introduced to recruit faculty members at all levels and outstanding scholars are invited to join the University under the SHS. Appointees recruited under the SHS should have conducted / led world-leading research that is commensurate with the stage of their academic career.\u00a0 Faculty members recruited through SHS at Chair Professor or Professor level will receive a start-up grant of HKD 5 million or more to support research activities (including the admission of two PhD students, purchase of equipment, hiring of research staff, etc.) in the initial five years, whereas those appointed at Associate Professor or Assistant Professor level will receive a start-up grant of HKD 3 million or more. For more information about PolyU, FCE and its constituent academic units, please visit PolyU\u2019s website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk . Duties The appointees will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0undertake teaching duties at various levels in the above architecture related areas; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0engage in programme and curriculum planning, development, validation, accreditation and administration of architecture-related programmes; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0supervise undergraduate and postgraduate research projects and theses; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0initiate and lead scholarly research projects in their areas of expertise, actively pursue quality journal publications, and seek external research grants to enhance the Department\u2019s research strengths; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0undertake relevant administrative duties; and (f)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Dean and the Head of Unit or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0have a bachelor degree in Architectural Studies and a master\u2019s degree in Architecture or equivalent, leading to an architect professional qualification; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0have a PhD degree in Architecture, Architectural Engineering, Urban Planning, Landscape Design or a related discipline; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0 be a registered architect in Hong Kong and a member of the Hong Kong Institute of Architects or equivalent; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0have knowledge of advanced technology related to Architecture and Design, including proficiency in BIM, Revit and other relevant tools; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0have substantial years of relevant post-qualification experience, in particular programme development and management; (f)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0have a strong commitment to excellence in teaching and research; (g)\u00a0 \u00a0 have an excellent proven record in research and scholarship achievement; and (h) \u00a0 \u00a0be able to demonstrate effective classroom teaching skills and have good interpersonal skills. Applicants for appointment at Chair Professor level should have an outstanding record of global leadership and research achievement in the community, in addition to substantial years of relevant post-qualification experience. Applicants for appointment at Professor or Associate Professor level should have a substantial number of years of experience and an excellent record of relevant academic and/or research achievement in the specified field. Applicants with less experience will be considered for appointment at the level of Assistant Professor. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered. \u00a0Initial appointment for Assistant Professor will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.\u00a0 Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement.\u00a0\u00a0An appropriate term will be provided for appointment at\u00a0Associate Professor / Professor / Chair Professor levels.\u00a0 For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . Consideration of applications will commence on 1 December 2025 until the positions are filled . Apply Now Posting date: 11 November 2025 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=261026009": {"title": "Visiting Lecturer (Part-time)", "description": "Job Application - Visiting Lecturer (Part-time) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Construction Management and Intelligence Visiting Lecturer (Part-time) (Ref. 261026009) [Appointment period: from January 2027 to May 2027] Duties The appointee will be required to teach weekend subject for taught postgraduate degree level students on \u201cManaging People in Projects (BRE5731)\u201d during Semester 2 of the 2026/2027 academic year. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0a master\u2019s degree with at least three years of post-qualification teaching / research / practical / industrial experience in a related discipline; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0a good command of written and spoken English; and (c) \u00a0 \u00a0good communication skills. Preference will be given to those with doctoral degree and corporate membership of relevant professional bodies, e.g. HKIS, HKIE or HKIA. Conditions of Service The remuneration rate is HK$1,100 per hour. The closing date for application is 14 November 2026. Apply Now Posting date: 26 October 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=261026008": {"title": "Visiting Lecturer (Part-time)", "description": "Job Application - Visiting Lecturer (Part-time) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Construction Management and Intelligence Visiting Lecturer (Part-time) (Ref. 261026008) [Appointment period: from January 2027 to May 2027] Duties The appointee will be required to teach weekday daytime subject for undergraduate degree level students on \u201cApplied Property Valuation (BRE436)\u201d during Semester 2 of the 2026/2027 academic year. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0a master\u2019s degree with at least three years of post-qualification teaching / research / practical / industrial experience in a related discipline; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0a good command of written and spoken English; and (c) \u00a0 \u00a0good communication skills. Preference will be given to those with doctoral degree and corporate membership of relevant professional bodies, e.g. HKIS, HKIE or HKIA. Conditions of Service The remuneration rate is HK$1,100 per hour. The closing date for application is 14 November 2026. Apply Now Posting date: 26 October 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=261026007": {"title": "Visiting Lecturer (Part-time)", "description": "Job Application - Visiting Lecturer (Part-time) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Construction Management and Intelligence Visiting Lecturer (Part-time) (Ref. 261026007) [Appointment period: from January 2027 to May 2027] Duties The appointee will be required to teach weekday daytime subject for undergraduate degree level students on \u201cLegal Context of Construction & Real Estate (BRE206)\u201d during Semester 2 of the 2026/2027 academic year. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0a master\u2019s degree with at least three years of post-qualification teaching / research / practical / industrial experience in a related discipline; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0a good command of written and spoken English; and (c) \u00a0 \u00a0good communication skills. Preference will be given to those with doctoral degree and corporate membership of relevant professional bodies, e.g. HKIS, HKIE or HKIA. Conditions of Service The remuneration rate is HK$1,100 per hour. The closing date for application is 14 November 2026. Apply Now Posting date: 26 October 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=261021014": {"title": "Chair Professor / Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Atmospheric Chemistry and Modelling under Strategic Hiring Scheme", "description": "Job Application - Chair Professor / Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Atmospheric Chemistry and Modelling under Strategic Hiring Scheme Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering Chair Professor / Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Atmospheric Chemistry and Modelling under Strategic Hiring Scheme (Ref. 261021014) The Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering at PolyU enjoys a high international reputation in conducting world-class research for societal benefits and has well established partnerships with the industry and government agencies in Hong Kong and beyond. It is ranked the 2nd best worldwide in Civil Engineering in the U.S. News Best Global Universities Rankings 2026, the 18th in Civil and Structural Engineering and the 34th in Environmental Science in the QS World University Rankings by Subject 2026 (both ranked No. 1 in Hong Kong). The Department offers academic programmes at various levels (PhD, MSC, BEng, BSc). The Department currently has about 80 faculty members (more than 40 regular faculty members at Assistant Professor and above levels) and around 40 technical and administrative personnel, and is committed to international standards of excellence in teaching and research. Please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/cee/ for more information about the Department. The Hong Kong Special Administrative Region is an international city located strategically at the heart of Asia and is the gateway to Chinese Mainland, with excellent transport links to major international cities. The Department is seeking a highly motivated and suitably qualified individual with research expertise in atmospheric chemistry or physics, AI-driven or process-based atmospheric modelling, health impacts of air pollution, or other related disciplines. To boost the leadership and impact of PolyU\u2019s research work in areas of significant societal needs and strategic importance, the Strategic Hiring Scheme is introduced to recruit faculty members at all levels and outstanding scholars are invited to join the University under the Strategic Hiring Scheme.\u00a0 Appointees recruited under the Strategic Hiring Scheme should have conducted / led world-leading research that is commensurate with the stage of their academic career. Duties The appointees will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0teach at undergraduate and postgraduate levels in related disciplines; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0conduct research that leads to publications in top-tier refereed journals and awards of \u00a0 research grants; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0undertake research, programme / curriculum development and administration; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0supervise student projects and theses; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0engage in industrial and scholarly research / consultancy activities; (f)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0undertake academic and departmental administrative duties; and (g) \u00a0 \u00a0perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Unit or his delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0a PhD in Engineering or Science, specialising in Environmental / Atmospheric Sciences, Air Pollution Control, or a related field; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0a strong commitment to excellence in teaching and research; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0strong records of research, publications and scholarship in atmospheric chemistry and \u00a0 physics, atmospheric modelling, or air pollution control technology; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0good networking ability and excellent potential to become a world-leading scholar; and (e) \u00a0 \u00a0excellent communication skills and the ability to use English as the medium of instruction. Applicants for appointment at Chair Professor level should have an outstanding record of global leadership and research achievement in the community, in addition to substantial years of relevant post-qualification experience. Applicants for appointment at Professor or Associate Professor level should have a substantial number of years of experience and an excellent record of relevant academic and/or research achievement in the specified field. Applicants with less experience will be considered for appointment at the level of Assistant Professor. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered. \u00a0Faculty members recruited through the Strategic Hiring Scheme at Chair Professor or Professor level will receive a start-up grant of HKD 5 million or more to support research activities (including the admission of two PhD students, purchase of equipment, hiring of research staff, etc.) in the initial five years, whereas those appointed at Associate Professor or Assistant Professor level will receive a start-up grant of HKD 3 million or more.\u00a0 Initial appointment for Assistant Professor will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.\u00a0 Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement.\u00a0\u00a0An appropriate term will be provided for appointment at Associate Professor / Professor / Chair Professor levels.\u00a0 For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . C onsideration of applications will commence on 20 November 2026 until the positions are filled . Apply Now Posting date: 21 October 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=261021009": {"title": "Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Intelligent Railway Engineering under Strategic Hiring Scheme", "description": "Job Application - Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Intelligent Railway Engineering under Strategic Hiring Scheme Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Home External Advertisements Open / close back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Intelligent Railway Engineering under Strategic Hiring Scheme (Ref. 261021009) The Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering (CEE) and the Hong Kong Branch of National Rail Transit Electrification and Automation Engineering Technology Research Center (CNERC-Rail) invite applications from highly motivated and suitably qualified candidates with research expertise in intelligent railway technologies, including smart materials and structures, railway monitoring and control, and intelligent maintenance of rail infrastructure. The Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering has a strong international reputation for conducting world-class research that delivers societal benefits and maintains well-established partnerships with industry and government agencies in Hong Kong and beyond. It is ranked first worldwide in Transportation Science and Technology in the Shanghai-Ranking Global Ranking of Academic Subjects 2025, the 2nd in Civil Engineering in the U.S. News Best Global Universities Rankings 2026, the 18th in Civil and Structural Engineering, and 34th in Environmental Science in the QS World University Rankings by Subject 2026. The Department offers academic programmes at the various levels (PhD, MSc, BEng, BSc). \u00a0It currently comprises approximately 80 faculty members (more than 40 regular faculty members at Assistant Professor or above levels) and around 40 technical and administrative staff. \u00a0The Department is committed to internationally recognised standards of excellence in teaching and research. \u00a0For further information about CEE, please visit https://www.polyu.edu.hk/cee/ . CNERC-Rail is a national-level, mission-driven innovation hub dedicated to advancing safer, smarter and lower-carbon rail transit systems. Building on The Hong Kong Polytechnic University\u2019s established strengths and global reputation in rail transit, intelligent infrastructure and smart cities, the Center collaborates with industry partners, government agencies and leading universities in the Chinese Mainland and worldwide to conduct pioneering research and translate research outcomes into practical applications. The Center aspires to become a world-leading research and development hub for intelligent operation and maintenance technologies and a major platform for developing talent in related fields. \u00a0For further information about the Center, please visit https://www.polyu.edu.hk/cnerc-rail/ . The Hong Kong Special Administrative Region is an international city located strategically at the heart of Asia and is the gateway to the Chinese Mainland, with excellent transport links to major international cities. To boost the leadership and impact of PolyU\u2019s research work in areas of significant societal needs and strategic importance, the Strategic Hiring Scheme is introduced to recruit faculty members at all levels and outstanding scholars are invited to join the University under the Strategic Hiring Scheme.\u00a0 Appointees recruited under the Strategic Hiring Scheme should have conducted / led world-leading research that is commensurate with the stage of their academic career. Duties The appointee will be affiliated with the Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering and serve as a key member of CNERC-Rail, with the potential to assume a future leadership role as Director or Associate Director of the Center. \u00a0The appointee will lead the development and delivery of new postgraduate programmes in Railway Engineering or Transportation Engineering. \u00a0The appointee will be required to: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0teach undergraduate and postgraduate subjects in Railway Engineering and related fields, such as Transit Engineering, Intelligent Infrastructure, Transportation Engineering, Sensing and Monitoring, Energy Systems, and Artificial Intelligence for Infrastructure; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0conduct high-impact research that leads to publications in top-tier refereed journals, and actively pursue and secure competitive research funding; (c) \u00a0 \u00a0initiate, lead and participate in mission-driven research programmes aligned with CNERC-Rail\u2019s objectives, including the development and commercialisation of prototypes, pilot projects and digital-twin platforms; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0supervise student projects and MSc and PhD dissertations; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0participate in scholarly, industrial and consultancy activities, including collaborations with rail transit equipment manufacturers, operators, government agencies and international partners; (f)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0contribute, where appropriate, to innovation and knowledge-transfer activities; (g) \u00a0 \u00a0undertake academic and administrative duties at the Center, Department and University levels; (h) \u00a0 \u00a0develop and manage subjects, curricula and pedagogical approaches for existing and new postgraduate programmes; and (i) \u00a0 \u00a0 perform any other duties assigned by the Director of CNERC-Rail, Head of Unit or their delegates. Qualifications Applicants should possess: (a) \u00a0 \u00a0a PhD in Railway, Civil, Transportation, Mechanical, Electrical or Electronic Engineering, Materials Science, Computer or Data Science, or a closely related discipline, which is relevant to Rail Transit Electrification, Automation, Sensing, Intelligent Operation and Maintenance, or related areas; (b) \u00a0 \u00a0expertise in, but not limited to, one or more of the following areas: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0high-sensitivity flexible sensors for rail transit applications (e.g. transient pressure, structural stress, wind loads, tunnel\u2013bridge dynamic loads), including sensor networks and digital twins for full life-cycle health monitoring and early warning; \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0energy harvesting devices and acoustic\u2013electric conversion metamaterials, specifically for harvesting railway noise and vibration energy in trains, tracks, and tunnels; \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0surface metamaterials / metastructures for drag reduction and aeroacoustic noise mitigation, including CFD-based design and machine-learning-driven optimisation of microstructured and bio-inspired surfaces; \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0carbon\u2013cement batteries and supercapacitors, including cement-based structural capacitors, multifunctional energy-storage/binding materials, and data-driven materials discovery using machine learning and large language models; and \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0intelligent operation and maintenance systems for rail infrastructure and networks, including digital twins, multimodal sensing, AI-powered diagnostics and prognostics, predictive maintenance, and full life-cycle asset management for track and electrification systems. (c)\u00a0 \u00a0 a strong record of high-quality, high-impact research in one or more of the areas listed above, demonstrated through achievements such as journal publications, competitive research grants, patents, prototypes or industrial collaborations; (d) \u00a0 \u00a0a strong commitment to excellence in teaching, research and knowledge application; (e) \u00a0 \u00a0demonstrated ability, or strong potential, to establish an independent, externally funded research programme and to lead or contribute to interdisciplinary, industry-engaged research projects; (f)\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0strong professional networks and the potential to become a world-leading scholar and academic leader within CNERC-Rail; and (g) \u00a0 \u00a0excellent communication skills and a high level of proficiency in English for teaching and presentations. Applicants for appointment as Professor should demonstrate excellence in teaching, an outstanding international research reputation, and proven experience in leading academic teams. Applicants with less experience may be considered for appointment as Associate Professor or Assistant Professor. \u00a0Duties and performance expectations will be commensurate with the level of appointment. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered. \u00a0Faculty members recruited through the Strategic Hiring Scheme at Professor level will receive a start-up grant of HKD 5 million or more to support research activities (including the admission of two PhD students, purchase of equipment, hiring of research staff, etc.) in the initial five years, whereas those appointed at Associate Professor or Assistant Professor level will receive a start-up grant of HKD 3 million or more.\u00a0 Initial appointment for Assistant Professor will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.\u00a0 Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement.\u00a0\u00a0An appropriate term will be provided for appointment at Associate Professor / Professor levels.\u00a0 For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . C onsideration of applications will commence on 20 November 2026 until the position is filled . Apply Now Posting date: 21 October 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright \u00a9 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved."}}, "rows": {"https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260925018": {"school_id": 1844, "posting_url": "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260925018", "job_title_in_post": "Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Design (two posts)", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor; Associate_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "School of Design, a leading and transdisciplinary design school, is", "area_key_words": "Design", "deadline_of_application": "31 October 2026", "posted_date": "25 September 2026", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260921002": {"school_id": 1844, "posting_url": "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260921002", "job_title_in_post": "Associate Professor in Fashion and Textile Technology", "position_type": "Associate_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "School of Fashion and Textiles Associate Professor in Fashion and Textile Technology", "area_key_words": "Fashion and Textile Technology", "deadline_of_application": "30 September 2026", "posted_date": "21 September 2026", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260915003": {"school_id": 1844, "posting_url": "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260915003", "job_title_in_post": "Chair Professor / Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Sustainable Ocean Science and Engineering under Strategic Hiring Scheme", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor; Associate_Professor; Full_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering", "area_key_words": "Sustainable Ocean Science and Engineering under Strategic Hiring Scheme; Hydrological Engineering; Marine Technology", "deadline_of_application": "14 October 2026", "posted_date": "15 September 2026", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260904007": {"school_id": 1844, "posting_url": "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260904007", "job_title_in_post": "Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Hospitality Managem